{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788226457821,"sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_6b500d0db1af451189cb05e4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"source venv/bin/activate && python --version && pip list 2>/dev/null && which python"},"output":"Python 3.12.12\nPackage    Version\n---------- -------\ncoverage   7.16.0\niniconfig  2.3.0\npackaging  26.3\npip        25.0.1\npluggy     1.6.0\nPygments   2.21.0\npytest     9.1.1\npytest-cov 7.1.0\n/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/venv/bin/python\n","metadata":{"output":"Python 3.12.12\nPackage    Version\n---------- -------\ncoverage   7.16.0\niniconfig  2.3.0\npackaging  26.3\npip        25.0.1\npluggy     1.6.0\nPygments   2.21.0\npytest     9.1.1\npytest-cov 7.1.0\n/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/venv/bin/python\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"source venv/bin/activate && python --version && pip list 2>/dev/null && which python","time":{"start":1788226457818,"end":1788226457820}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I understand the data. Let me check the Python environment and what packages are available:\n\n1. Check venv packages\n2. Check python version\n\nThen plan the implementation:\n\n**Architecture:**\n- `src/brasil_mcp/` package:\n  - `__init__.py`\n  - `models.py` — dataclasses for Match, Player, TeamStats, etc.\n  - `normalize.py` — team name normalization (accents, state suffixes, full names → canonical)\n  - `loaders.py` — CSV loaders for the 6 files\n  - `store.py` / `db.py` — in-memory \"knowledge graph\" repository combining all match datasets + players\n  - `queries.py` — query functions: match queries, team stats, head-to-head, standings, players, aggregates\n  - `server.py` — MCP server exposing tools\n  - `cli.py` — optional CLI for direct queries / demo\n- `tests/` — BDD-style pytest (Given/When/Then structure)\n- `requirements.txt`, `pyproject.toml`\n- `README.md` update\n\nFor the MCP server, I should check if `mcp` package is installed or installable. The environment may be offline. Let me check.\n\nKey design considerations:\n1. Team name normalization — critical. Names like \"Palmeiras-SP\", \"Palmeiras\", \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\", \"Corinthians\", \"Athletico-PR\", \"Atlético-PR\", \"Atletico Paranaense\" etc. Also unaccenting. Also BR-Football-Dataset has names like \"Sao Paulo\" (no accents). And Copa do Brasil has \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\".\n\n2. Date parsing — ISO, Brazilian format, with times.\n\n3. The match datasets overlap (Brasileirão matches appear in both Brasileirao_Matches.csv, novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv, and BR-Football-Dataset.csv). For head-to-head queries and team stats, we need to decide whether to use a specific dataset or all. I'll design a unified match store where each match carries a source/competition, and queries can filter by competition and source. Default: query across all matches (dedupe? maybe not necessary; but head-to-head from Brasileirão file specifically might be desirable). Actually the spec example: \"Head-to-head in dataset: Flamengo 12 wins, ...\" — they compute within what's found. I'll provide a `source` filter parameter.\n\n4. Standings — calculate from match results per season per competition. For Brasileirão Serie A, standings can be computed for seasons 2003-2019 (novo) and 2012-2023 (Brasileirao_Matches). Note 2020 season in Brasileirao_Matches? Let me check the seasons present. Also points: 3 for win, 1 draw.\n\n5. FIFA data: filter by Nationality == \"Brazil\", Club contains team name, positions.\n\n6. MCP server: use the `mcp` Python SDK with FastMCP if available; otherwise implement a minimal JSON-RPC stdio MCP server myself. Let me check what's installed. The instruction says \"Make sure the code builds and tests pass.\" The venv has pytest and coverage. Let me check pip list.\n\nLet me check the environment first.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05a9a4ff7001uqGqglagiv6xsx","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05a9a0465001dNysxqNwit0PjM"}}
