{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788226844408,"sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_1bb17bb15dda43638e491177","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"source venv/bin/activate && python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, collections\n\ndef load(path):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nbrf = load('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\nsa23 = [r for r in brf if r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'].startswith('2023')]\nprint('Serie A 2023 in brf:', len(sa23))\nteams23 = collections.Counter()\nfor r in sa23: teams23[r['home']]+=1\nprint('teams:', len(teams23), 'home games each:', set(teams23.values()))\n# Palmeiras 2023 record\nimport unicodedata\ndef sa(x): return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFKD',x) if not unicodedata.combining(c))\nw=d=l=gf=ga=0\nfor r in sa23:\n    if 'Palmeiras' in (r['home'], r['away']):\n        hg,ag=int(float(r['home_goal'])),int(float(r['away_goal']))\n        if r['home']=='Palmeiras':\n            gf+=hg; ga+=ag\n            w+= hg>ag; d+= hg==ag; l+= hg<ag\n        else:\n            gf+=ag; ga+=hg\n            w+= ag>hg; d+= ag==hg; l+= ag<hg\nprint('Palmeiras 2023 Série A:', w,d,l,gf,ga)\n\n# foreign suffixes in Libertadores\nlib = load('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv')\nsufs = collections.Counter()\nimport re\nfor r in lib:\n    for t in (r['home_team'], r['away_team']):\n        m = re.search(r'-([A-Za-z]{2,4})$', t) or re.search(r'\\(([A-Z]{2,4})\\)', t)\n        if m: sufs[m.group(1)] += 1\nprint('lib suffixes:', sufs.most_common(20))\n\n# check Santa Cruz & derby teams presence in all data\nallnames = set()\nfor r in brf: allnames.update([r['home'], r['away']])\nnovo = load('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nfor r in novo: allnames.update([r['Equipe_mandante'], r['Equipe_visitante']])\nfor t in ['Santa Cruz','Bragantino','Red Bull Bragantino','Coritiba','Vitória','Bahia','Ceará','Fortaleza','Athletico Paranaense','Atletico Goianiense','Vasco']:\n    print(t, any(sa(t).lower() in sa(n).lower() for n in allnames))\nEOF"},"output":"Serie A 2023 in brf: 377\nteams: 20 home games each: {18, 19}\nPalmeiras 2023 Série A: 19 10 8 61 32\nlib suffixes: [('PAR', 110), ('MG', 82), ('URU', 74), ('EQU', 48), ('Colo', 34), ('PR', 14), ('PER', 12), ('VEN', 6)]\nSanta Cruz True\nBragantino True\nRed Bull Bragantino False\nCoritiba True\nVitória True\nBahia True\nCeará True\nFortaleza True\nAthletico Paranaense True\nAtletico Goianiense True\nVasco True\n","metadata":{"output":"Serie A 2023 in brf: 377\nteams: 20 home games each: {18, 19}\nPalmeiras 2023 Série A: 19 10 8 61 32\nlib suffixes: [('PAR', 110), ('MG', 82), ('URU', 74), ('EQU', 48), ('Colo', 34), ('PR', 14), ('PER', 12), ('VEN', 6)]\nSanta Cruz True\nBragantino True\nRed Bull Bragantino False\nCoritiba True\nVitória True\nBahia True\nCeará True\nFortaleza True\nAthletico Paranaense True\nAtletico Goianiense True\nVasco True\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"source venv/bin/activate && python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, collections\n\ndef load(path):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nbrf = load('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\nsa23 = [r for r in brf if r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'].startswith('2023')]\nprint('Serie A 2023 in brf:', len(sa23))\nteams23 = collections.Counter()\nfor r in sa23: teams23[r['home']]+=1\nprint('teams:', len(teams23), 'home games each:', set(teams23.values()))\n# Palmeiras 2023 record\nimport unicodedata\ndef sa(x): return ''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFKD',x) if not unicodedata.combining(c))\nw=d=l=gf=ga=0\nfor r in sa23:\n    if 'Palmeiras' in (r['home'], r['away']):\n        hg,ag=int(float(r['home_goal'])),int(float(r['away_goal']))\n        if r['home']=='Palmeiras':\n            gf+=hg; ga+=ag\n            w+= hg>ag; d+= hg==ag; l+= hg<ag\n        else:\n            gf+=ag; ga+=hg\n            w+= ag>hg; d+= ag==hg; l+= ag<hg\nprint('Palmeiras 2023 Série A:', w,d,l,gf,ga)\n\n# foreign suffixes in Libertadores\nlib = load('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv')\nsufs = collections.Counter()\nimport re\nfor r in lib:\n    for t in (r['home_team'], r['away_team']):\n        m = re.search(r'-([A-Za-z]{2,4})$', t) or re.search(r'\\(([A-Z]{2,4})\\)', t)\n        if m: sufs[m.group(1)] += 1\nprint('lib suffixes:', sufs.most_common(20))\n\n# check Santa Cruz & derby teams presence in all data\nallnames = set()\nfor r in brf: allnames.update([r['home'], r['away']])\nnovo = load('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nfor r in novo: allnames.update([r['Equipe_mandante'], r['Equipe_visitante']])\nfor t in ['Santa Cruz','Bragantino','Red Bull Bragantino','Coritiba','Vitória','Bahia','Ceará','Fortaleza','Athletico Paranaense','Atletico Goianiense','Vasco']:\n    print(t, any(sa(t).lower() in sa(n).lower() for n in allnames))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788226844398,"end":1788226844403}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"`mcp.shared.memory.create_client_server_memory_streams` is available for in-memory integration tests.\n\nNow let me set up the project. Plan:\n\n```\npyproject.toml          # package config (setuptools), deps, pytest config\nrequirements.txt\nsrc/brasil_mcp/\n  __init__.py\n  dates.py\n  normalize.py\n  models.py\n  loaders.py\n  store.py\n  queries.py        # formatted answers built on store\n  derbies.py        # curated derby pairs (could live in store/queries)\n  server.py         # MCP server (v2 MCPServer)\n  cli.py\ntests/\n  conftest.py\n  test_dates.py\n  test_normalize.py\n  test_loaders.py\n  test_bdd_match_queries.py\n  test_bdd_team_queries.py\n  test_bdd_player_queries.py\n  test_bdd_competition_queries.py\n  test_bdd_statistics.py\n  test_server.py\nrun_server.py?      # or console_script entry point `brasil-soccer-mcp`\n```\n\nLet me now write all the code. Start with pyproject + package modules.\n\n**dates.py**: parse_date(s) handling: \"2012-05-19 18:30:00\", \"2023-09-24\", \"29/03/2003\", \"NA\", empty → None. Return datetime.date. Also parse_time.\n\n**normalize.py**:\n- `strip_accents`\n- `BRAZILIAN_UFS` set of 27 abbreviations.\n- `ALIASES`: dict mapping normalized alias → (base, uf). Entries for full/official names:\n  - 'sport club corinthians paulista' → ('corinthians','SP')\n  - 'corinthians' → ('corinthians','SP')? no — bare names resolved via registry dominance, but for bases with multiple ufs I pin defaults in DEFAULT_UF. Let me structure:\n    - `parse_team_name(raw)` → (base, uf_or_None, country_tag_or_None)\n      Steps: strip accents → lower; extract parenthetical: if '(xxx)' matches 3 uppercase letters (in original raw?) treat as country code; remove all parentheticals; replace non-alnum (except '-' and space) with space; split on '-' → tokens; if last token is 2-letter UF → uf; elif last token 3 letters and (original had it uppercase after '-') → country code (e.g., 'EQU'). Handle ' - RJ' spacing (cup format \"América - MG\"). Also handle names ending ' MG' word form (brf: 'America MG', 'Gremio RS').\n      Then remove filler words: {'sport','club','esporte','clube','de','regatas','do','da','futebol','fc','ec','sc','athletic'?} — careful: 'Sport' alone (Sport-PE)! If I remove 'sport' filler, 'Sport - PE' → base '' + uf PE. Disaster. So filler removal must only strip these words when base would remain non-empty AND only in specific patterns: leading \"sport club\", \"esporte clube\", \"clube de regatas\", \"grêmio fbpa\" etc. Safer: alias-table driven for full names, and only strip filler words if the remaining base is non-empty and the phrase matches known legal-name patterns like r'^sport club (.+)$' → keep captured part unless captured is 'paulista'?? \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" → 'corinthians paulista' → hmm, contains 'paulista' (city adjective). I want base 'corinthians'. My alias table handles the famous full names explicitly. Pattern rules (ordered):\n        1. exact alias table hit (on normalized full string) → (base, uf)\n        2. pattern r'^(sport club|sporting club|esporte clube|clube atl[ée]tico|clube de regatas|athletic club)?\\s*(?P<rest>.+)$' — too fuzzy. I'll rely on: strip filler tokens {sport, club, esporte, clube, regatas, atletico?} NO.\n        \n      Simpler robust approach: token-filter: remove tokens in FILLER = {'sport','club','clube','esporte','regatas','futebol','athletic','fc','ec','sc','ac','bbc','aa','cr'} ONLY IF at least one non-filler token remains. Then 'sport club corinthians paulista' → 'corinthians paulista'. Then trailing city adjectives? 'paulista' → map to SP uf if no uf yet? 'corinthians paulista' base... I want 'corinthians'. Add WORD_UF map: trailing tokens {'paulista':'SP','carioca':'RJ','mineiro':'MG','paranaense':'PR','gaúcho/gaucho':'RS','baiano':'BA','pernambucano':'PE','cearense':'CE','goiano':'GO'...} extracted as uf when at end. 'corinthians paulista' → uf SP, base 'corinthians'. 'atlético paranaense' → uf PR, base 'atletico'. 'atlético mineiro' → uf MG, base 'atletico'. 'atletico goiano'? not used. But careful: 'Vitória' → base 'vitoria' fine. 'América FC (Minas Gerais)' → parenthetical '(minas gerais)' not a country code — just drop parentheticals that aren't country codes; tokens: 'america fc' → filter 'fc' → 'america'. No uf → registry dominance: america has ufs MG, RN... ambiguous! FIFA 'América FC (Minas Gerais)' would resolve to dominant uf (RN or MG by match count?). Need alias: 'america fc (minas gerais)' — but I drop the parens. Better: keep parenthetical content as tokens when not a country code: '(minas gerais)' → tokens 'minas gerais' → map 'minas gerais' → MG uf! So 'america fc minas gerais' → uf MG (from state-name words), base 'america'. \n      \n      So WORD_UF includes state names and adjectives: {'minas gerais':'MG','sao paulo':'SP'? no! 'São Paulo' is a team name itself — can't treat 'sao paulo' as uf tag blindly. But 'América de São Paulo'? doesn't exist. Hmm, risky: team named 'São Paulo' base 'sao paulo'. If I strip 'sao paulo' as uf tag from other names — no other name contains 'sao paulo' except... 'São Paulo FC' → filter 'fc' → 'sao paulo' → base 'sao paulo' + no uf. But if WORD_UF extraction runs, 'sao paulo' → uf SP and base '' — must only apply WORD_UF when base remains non-empty. 'sao paulo' → applying gives base '' → don't apply. Good rule: extract trailing uf-word only if remaining base non-empty.\n      'rio de janeiro':'RJ', 'rio grande do sul':'RS', 'minas gerais':'MG', 'pernambuco':'PE', 'bahia':'BA'?? 'Bahia' is a club name! 'Esporte Clube Bahia' → filter → 'bahia' base. WORD_UF 'bahia' would break it: apply only if base non-empty after removal → 'bahia' alone stays base 'bahia'. OK, but is the rule \"trailing only\"? 'Bahia de Feira' → base 'bahia de feira'... trailing 'bahia'? no, trailing extraction takes LAST tokens; 'bahia de feira' last token 'feira'. fine.\n      Adjectives: paulista, carioca, mineiro, paranaense, gaucho, baiano, cearense, goiano, potiguar (RN), amazonense (AM), maranhense? (juventude ma? no that's 'Juventude - MA' suffix), matogrossense (MT), paraense (PA), piauiense (PI), alagoano (AL), sergipano (SE), paraibano (PB), capixaba (ES), catarinense (SC, 'avai catarinense'? no), brasiliense (DF — also a club name 'Brasiliense'! trailing extraction: 'brasiliense' alone → base '' → stays club). Distinct enough.\n\n      3. Suffix tokens: after tokenization, check trailing token: if in UF set (2-letter) → uf; if 3-letter all-alpha and original raw had it as uppercase suffix after '-' → country code (EQU, URU, PAR, MEX, ARG, CHI, COL, BOL, VEN, ECU...). Wait 'Barcelona-EQU' — EQU = Ecuador. And 'Guaraní (PAR)'. I'll collect the actual set from data. Also 'The Strongest (BOL)' etc.\n\n  - Registry: built from all match team names + FIFA clubs + alias entries. base→Counter(uf). Country-tagged names keep their tag in canonical id (e.g., 'nacional-uru') — separate club; display 'Nacional (URU)'.\n  - `resolve_team(raw)` → canonical id like 'palmeiras-sp' or 'flamengo-rj' or 'boca juniors' (no uf) or 'nacional-uru' (country).\n  - `display_name(canonical_id)` → nice display.\n  - DEFAULT_UF pins for ambiguous bare bases: 'juventude'→RS? wait juventude ma is Juventude-MA (Maranhão) vs juventude rs. Bare 'Juventude' appears in brf+novo — check which. brf 'Juventude' bare — Serie B Juventude-RS presumably; 'Juventude MA' separately. novo 'Juventude' = RS. So dominance → RS naturally. 'nautico' → PE vs RR: bras/cup PE; brf RR + cup RR. PE count: bras (multiple seasons Série A) + cup; RR: brf Serie C + cup. PE likely wins. 'santos' → SP vs AP: bare 'santos' in brf/lib/novo (many), 'santos ap' few → SP. 'nacional' → 'Nacional AM' brf/cup vs lib 'Nacional (URU)'/'Nacional (MEX)'? country-tagged stay separate; bare 'nacional'? Might appear in brf as Nacional-AM. → AM dominance fine.\n  - 'America' bare: brf 'America FC Natal'?? saw 'America FC Natal' in brf home teams! That's América-RN. And bare 'America'? Maybe in brf as 'America' (which one?). Let me check during registry build — I'll print ambiguous bases and pin as needed.\n\n- `normalize_team_query(raw)` for user queries: resolve via registry; if unknown, return None (tool reports \"team not found\" with suggestions via fuzzy: prefix/containment over known names).\n\n**models.py**: dataclasses Match, Player, TeamRecord, StandingEntry, plus result helper (`result_for(team)` → 'W'/'D'/'L').\n\nMatch fields: source, competition, season, date (date|None), time (str|None), round (str|None), stage (str|None), home, away (canonical ids), home_display, away_display, home_goals, away_goals (int|None), venue (str|None), home_state/away_state (str|None), stats: corners/shots/attacks (home/away, float|None), ht_result (str|None).\n\nPlayer fields: id, name, age, nationality, overall, potential, club, position, jersey, height, weight, preferred_foot, value, wage, plus a few skill attrs (finishing, dribbling, etc. as dict?). Keep selected columns; parse ints safely.\n\n**loaders.py**: functions per file returning (matches|players). Handle '-' goals → None. Handle 'NA' datetime. novo: parse 'Vencedor' not needed (compute). Arena → venue. BR-Football: floats → int; date; time; ht_result/at_result; tournament → competition mapping {'Serie A': 'Brasileirão Série A', 'Serie B': ..., 'Serie C': ..., 'Copa do Brasil': 'Copa do Brasil'}.\n\n**store.py**: SoccerStore: \n- __init__(data_dir): load all, build registry, matches list, dedupe index, team→match index (by canonical), players list, name→players index, club canonical → players.\n- competitions(): summary dict.\n- find_matches(...) with filters + dedupe (prefer source order).\n- head_to_head(a,b,...)\n- team_stats(...)\n- standings(season, competition)\n- biggest_wins(...), goals_analysis(...), best_records(...), team_season_history(...), derbies(...)\n- Dedupe: key (date, home, away, competition); if collision merge: prefer record with more non-null fields; keep first's source priority: order sources ['brasileirao','copa_do_brasil','libertadores','brasileirao_historico','br_football']? For Série A overlap 2012-2019: bras (2012-2022) vs novo (2003-2019) — prefer bras (has round+state); brf has stats — merge stats into kept record. I'll implement merge: kept = first by priority; then for dup, fill missing fields (venue, stats, time) from dup.\n\nPerformance: 24k matches total; in-memory filtering fine (<5s easily). Startup loads CSVs each server start (~1-2s for 18k players + 24k matches; fine). I'll also cache nothing on disk; keep simple. Actually loading fifa_data.csv 9MB with csv module ~0.5s. Fine.\n\n**queries.py**: formatted summaries (the \"Example answer format\" texts) + structured payloads. Each returns dict {'summary': str, ...fields}. Actually I'll put formatting inside store or a separate `formatting.py`. Let me keep `queries.py` with functions returning (dict) and formatting helpers there; server.py wraps them as tools; cli.py calls them too. \n\n**derbies**: curated pairs (canonical ids):\n- Fla-Flu: flamengo-rj × fluminense-rj\n- Clássico dos Milhões: flamengo-rj × vasco-rj\n- Majestoso: corinthians-sp × sao paulo-sp\n- Choque-Rei: palmeiras-sp × sao paulo-sp\n- Derby Paulista: palmeiras-sp × corinthians-sp\n- Grenal: internacional-rs × gremio-rs\n- Atletiba: atletico-pr × coritiba-pr\n- Clássico Vovô: botafogo-rj × fluminense-rj? (actually Vovô = Botafogo×Vasco; Clássico Vovô é Botafogo e Vasco... Let me get these right:\n  - Botafogo vs Vasco = \"Clássico Vovô\"? No — Botafogo vs Vasco is \"Clássico dos Gigantes\"? Hmm. Let me be careful:\n    - Fla-Flu = Flamengo × Fluminense ✓\n    - Clássico dos Milhões = Flamengo × Vasco ✓ (popularity)\n    - Majestoso = Corinthians × São Paulo ✓\n    - Choque-Rei = Palmeiras × São Paulo ✓ (some say Derby Paulista is Palmeiras × Corinthians ✓, and Choque-Rei Palmeiras × São Paulo ✓)\n    - Clássico Vovô = Botafogo × Fluminense (oldest derby in Brazil, 1905) — yes! Botafogo vs Fluminense is \"Vovô\". Wait no — Clássico Vovô is Botafogo × Fluminense (both founded 1904ish, first derby 1905). Yes that's right.\n    - Clássico da Amizade? Palmeiras × ... skip.\n    - Grenal = Grêmio × Internacional ✓\n    - Atletiba = Atlético-PR × Coritiba ✓\n    - Ba-Vi = Bahia × Vitória ✓\n    - Clássico-Rei = Fortaleza × Ceará ✓\n    - Clássico dos Clássicos = Santa Cruz × Sport? and Clássico das Emoções Náutico × Santa Cruz... In Recife: Clássico dos Clássicos = Sport × Santa Cruz; Clássico das Multidões = Sport × Náutico; Clássico das Emoções = Náutico × Santa Cruz. Include Sport-PE × Santa Cruz-PE (does Santa Cruz appear? check).\n    - Clássico da Serra? skip. Also \"Clássico Alvinegro\"? skip.\n    - Inter x Santos? no.\n  Check which canonical teams exist in data: santa cruz? criciúma? I'll include pairs conditionally on both teams existing in registry.\n\n**server.py**: MCPServer with tools. MCP 