t filler. 'Gremio FBPA'? not present. 'AA' e.g. 'AA Ponte Preta'? maybe. Keep FILLER = {'sport','club','clube','esporte','regatas','futebol','athletic','fc','ec','sc','ac','cr','aa','cbc','cec','sec','abc'?} — 'ABC' is a club (Natal)! Don't include 'abc'. Also 'ASA' club. Only include pure legal-entity words: sport? NO — 'Sport' alone is a club (Sport Recife). If I filter 'sport' and remaining is empty → keep as-is. My rule: filter filler tokens only if ≥1 token remains. 'Sport - PE' → tokens ['sport'], uf PE extracted first → after uf extraction tokens ['sport'] → filter would empty it → keep ['sport']. base 'sport' uf PE → sport-pe ✓. 'Sport Club do Recife' → tokens [sport, club, do, recife] → filter {sport, club, do}?? 'do' is a filler too (preposition). FILLER_PRE = {'do','da','de','dos','das'}. Remaining ['recife'] → base 'recife'?? That maps Sport Recife → 'recife' base. Hmm, but is there another 'recife' club? 'Náutico' is 'Náutico Capibaribe'... base 'recife' unique-ish. But display would be 'Recife' — wrong. Better: keep 'sport recife' → don't filter 'sport' when followed by other words? The issue: filtering 'sport' from 'Sport Club Corinthians Paulista' gives 'corinthians paulista' → with paulista→SP extraction → 'corinthians' ✓. For 'Sport Club do Recife' filtering gives 'recife' → want 'sport-pe'. \n  Solution: ALIAS table for official full names handles famous clubs:\n    'sport club do recife' → ('sport', 'PE')\n    'sport club corinthians paulista' → ('corinthians', 'SP')\n    'clube de regatas vasco da gama' / 'vasco da gama' → ('vasco', 'RJ')\n    'clube de regatas do flamengo' / 'flamengo' → handled bare\n    'atletico mineiro' → ('atletico','MG')\n    'atletico paranaense'/'athletico paranaense' → ('atletico','PR')\n    'america fc minas gerais' → ('america','MG')  [after paren removal tokens: america fc minas gerais; state-name words: 'minas gerais' → MG]\n    'ceara sporting club' → ('ceara','CE')\n    'sao paulo fc' → ('sao paulo','SP') (natura