maranhense':MA,'rondoniense':RO,'acreano':AC,'tocantinense':TO,'brasiliense':DF,'sul-mato-grossense':MS}. Apply only if remaining base non-empty. NOTE: 'mineiro' also appears in 'Atlético Mineiro' — alias handles that before adjective extraction? 'atletico mineiro' → alias hit first ✓. But what about 'Cruzeiro Esporte Clube'? natural. 'Vila Nova-GO' natural. What about club 'Operário-MS' etc. natural. 'Tuna Luso'? fine. 'Paysandu' fine. 'Nacional-AM' fine.\n8. Filter filler tokens (only if non-empty remains): FILLER = {'sport','club','clube','esporte','regatas','futebol','athletic','fc','ec','sc','ac','cr','fr','st','sao'? no!}. Wait — filtering 'sport' from 'santa cruz' no. From 'sport recife' → 'recife'. I decided alias-first. But unknown full names like 'Esporte Clube Vitória' → 'vitoria' ✓ good. 'Sport Club Internacional' → 'internacional' ✓. 'Guarani Esporte Clube'? (there are multiple Guarani clubs: Guarani-SP, Guarani de Juazeiro?) ambiguous anyway. OK filter with the guard.\n9. Spelling folds: 'athletico' → 'atletico'. Also 'criciuma'? natural. 'coritiba'? natural.\n10. If base empty after all → fall back to pre-filter tokens.\n\ncanonical(base, uf, country) = f\"{base}-{uf.lower()}\" or f\"{base}-{country.lower()}\" or base.\n\nRegistry resolution `resolve(raw)`:\n- parse → (base, uf, country).\n- If country → canonical base-country.\n- If uf → canonical base-uf.\n- If no uf: look up base in base_uf_counts (from all observed names): if exactly 1 uf → that. If multiple → DEFAULT pin table (for known ambiguous: {'santos':'SP','juventude':'RS','nautico':'PE','nacional':'AM','america':'MG','botafogo':'RJ','vitoria':'BA','parana':'PR','gremio':'RS','internacional':'RS','bahia':'BA','sport':'PE','coritiba':'PR','ceara':'CE','fortaleza':'CE','goias':'GO','figueirense':'SC','chapecoense':'SC','avai':'SC','criciuma':'SC','portuguesa':'SP','ponte preta':'SP','guarani':'SP','flamengo':'RJ','fluminense':'RJ','vasco':'RJ','corinthians':'SP','palmeiras':'SP','sao paulo':'SP','cruzeiro':'MG','atletico': 'MG'?}) — ambiguous 'atletico' bare! Where does bare 'Atletico' appear? Libertadores final row: 'Flamengo' vs 'Athletico' (the NA row). And maybe others in lib: 'Athletico' bare. So DEFAULT['atletico'] = 'PR' (Athletico-PR is the one in Libertadores). Also FIFA 'Atlético Mineiro'→alias, 'Atlético Paranaense'→alias — no bare 'atletico' there. Cup/bras always have suffixes. OK 'PR' default (Athletico). Also 'atletico goianiense' base distinct. \n  If base unknown entirely (no observations) → canonical = base alone (id as-is; unknown team).\n- Foreign clubs like 'boca juniors', 'river plate' → no uf → canonical base alone. Fine.\n\nAlso need `TEAM_ALIASES` map: normalized string → canonical id, used before pipeline (exact match on full normalized raw). And reverse: canonical id → display name (most frequent raw with accents preserved). I'll compute display from the most common raw name mapping to that canonical; prefer a raw with accents if tie... simplest: most frequent raw; if the most frequent is the '-SP' suffixed form (bras), display includes suffix. For big clubs display should be clean ('Palmeiras' not 'Palmeiras-SP'): choose, among raw variants, the most frequent one WITHOUT suffix if any variant lacks suffix; else suffixed form. E.g. palmeiras-sp: raws 'Palmeiras-SP' (bras 2012-2022 + cup) vs 'Palmeiras' (lib+novo+brf). Counts: cup matches many + bras 380*?; lib ~80; brf many Serie A 2014-2023 + novo 2003-2011 (9 seasons). Hmm, 'Palmeiras' unsuffixed count likely higher (novo 2003-2011: Palmeiras wasn't always in Série A... whatever, both fine). Rule: prefer unsuffixed when available AND when base unambiguous (single uf for base) → display 'Palmeiras'; when ambiguous base → always show suffix 'América-MG'. Deterministic and clean.\n\nFor 'sao paulo': base 'sao paulo' uf SP, unambiguous → 'São Paulo' (choose raw with original accents — pick the most frequent raw among unsuffixed; 'São Paulo' appears in novo/lib/brf-with-accents? brf uses 'Sao Paulo' ASCII. novo 'São Paulo' ✓).\n\nDisplay name selection algorithm: among raws for canonical: candidates_unsuffixed = raws whose parse has no uf; if base unambiguous and candidates_unsuffixed: pick most frequent; else pick most frequent overall. Keep original case/accents.\n\n### models.py\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass Match:\n    source: str\n    competition: str\n    season: int | None\n    date: date | None\n    time: str | None\n    round: str | None      #bras/cup/novo round number\n    stage: str | None      # libertadores stage / cup 'final' etc\n    home: str              # canonical id\n    away: str\n    home_display: str\n    away_display: str\n    home_goals: int | None\n    away_goals: int | None\n    venue: str | None\n    home_state: str | None\n    away_state: str | None\n    # optional stats\n    home_corners: int|None ... away_shots, home_attacks, away_attacks, ht_result, at_result, total_corners\n    @property def played, def score_str, def result_for(team), def winner...\n```\n\nPlayer:\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass Player:\n    id, name, age, nationality, overall, potential, club, club_canonical?, position, jersey, height, weight, preferred_foot, value, wage, skill: dict(str->int|None) for ~8 key skills (Crossing, Finishing, ... ), team? \n```\nclub_canonical resolved via registry (for team_players).\n\n### loaders.py\n\nLoader functions returning list[Match] (with canonical ids resolved later in store — loaders need registry? I'll have loaders produce raw dicts/dataclasses with raw names, and store does canonicalization via registry. Actually simpler: loaders take registry as arg and produce final Match objects. I'll pass registry into loaders.)\n\n- load_brasileirao(path, reg)\n- load_copa_do_brasil(path, reg)\n- load_libertadores(path, reg)\n- load_br_football(path, reg) — competition mapping via tournament col.\n- load_historico(path, reg)\n- load_fifa(path, reg)\n\nint parsing helper `to_int(v)`: handles '', 'NA', '-', '2.0' → 2.\n\n### store.py\n\nclass SoccerStore:\n- __init__(data_dir='data/kaggle')\n- registry, matches (list[Match]), deduped index built lazily per query? Dedupe at load: build dict key→Match with merge. `self.matches` = deduped list. Also keep self.duplicates count.\n  Merge policy: priority order source: brasileirao=0, copa_do_brasil=1, libertadores=2, brasileirao_historico=3, br_football=4. Keep lowest priority; enrich with fields from later dup (venue, stats, time, state).\n  Wait: brf has ht_result/at_result & stats; bras has round & states & time. For Série A overlap (bras ∩ brf 2014-2022): keep bras + fill stats from brf ✓. novo ∩ bras 2012-2019: keep bras (has datetime time, states) + fill venue from novo ✓. cup ∩ brf 'Copa do Brasil' 2014-2021: keep cup (has round) + fill stats ✓.\n- indexes: self._by_team: dict[canonical, list[idx]]; self._by_competition; players list; _players_by_name (lowercased full name); _players_by_club (canonical club); _club display.\n- methods:\n  - resolve_team(name) → canonical or None\n  - suggest_teams(name, n) → list of canonicals by containment\n  - find_matches(team=None, opponent=None, competition=None, season=None, date_from=None, date_to=None, stage=None, venue='any'|'home'|'away', limit=None, order='desc') → (matches, total_matching)\n  - head_to_head(a, b, competition=None) → dict with matches + summary\n  - team_stats(team, season=None, competition=None) → overall/home/away records + per-competition + per-season (recent seasons list)\n  - team_season_history(team, competition=None) → list per season\n  - standings(season, competition='Brasileirão Série A') → rows sorted, champion, relegated\n  - biggest_wins(competition=None, season=None, n=10)\n  - goals_analysis(competition=None, season=None) → matches, avg goals, home/away/draw rates, avg home/away goals\n  - best_records(competition=None, season=None, venue='overall', min_matches=10) → ranked teams by ppg/win rate\n  - competitions() → per competition: seasons