{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788227241872,"sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_39492c88e9a8437182889015","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"In-memory knowledge store unifying all match and player datasets.\n\nThe store loads the six CSVs once, deduplicates matches that appear in more\nthan one dataset (the 2012-2019 Série A seasons exist in three files), builds\nteam/player indexes, and exposes the query surface used by the MCP tools and\nthe CLI.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom datetime import date\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom .loaders import (\n    BR_FOOTBALL_TOURNAMENTS,\n    COPA_DO_BRASIL,\n    LIBERTADORES,\n    SERIE_A,\n    SERIE_B,\n    SERIE_C,\n    load_all,\n)\nfrom .models import Match, Player, TeamRecord\nfrom .normalize import TeamRegistry, normalize_text\n\nSOURCE_PRIORITY = {\n    \"brasileirao\": 0,\n    \"copa_do_brasil\": 1,\n    \"libertadores\": 2,\n    \"brasileirao_historico\": 3,\n    \"br_football\": 4,\n}\n\nCOMPETITION_ALIASES: list[tuple[tuple[str, ...], str]] = [\n    ((\"libertadores\", \"libertadora\"), LIBERTADORES),\n    ((\"copa do brasil\", \"copadobrasil\", \"cdb\", \"brazilian cup\"), COPA_DO_BRASIL),\n    ((\"serie b\", \"serieb\", \"serie b\", \"série b\", \"b series\"), SERIE_B),\n    ((\"serie c\", \"seriec\", \"série c\", \"c series\"), SERIE_C),\n    ((\"serie a\", \"seriea\", \"série a\", \"brasileirao\", \"brasileirão\", \"brasileirao serie a\"), SERIE_A),\n]\n\nDERBIES: list[tuple[str, str, str]] = [\n    (\"Fla-Flu\", \"flamengo-rj\", \"fluminense-rj\"),\n    (\"Clássico dos Milhões\", \"flamengo-rj\", \"vasco-rj\"),\n    (\"Clássico Vovô\", \"botafogo-rj\", \"fluminense-rj\"),\n    (\"Majestoso\", \"corinthians-sp\", \"sao paulo-sp\"),\n    (\"Choque-Rei\", \"palmeiras-sp\", \"sao paulo-sp\"),\n    (\"Derby Paulista\", \"palmeiras-sp\", \"corinthians-sp\"),\n    (\"Grenal\", \"gremio-rs\", \"internacional-rs\"),\n    (\"Atletiba\", \"atletico-pr\", \"coritiba-pr\"),\n    (\"Ba-Vi\", \"bahia-ba\", \"vitoria-ba\"),\n    (\"Clássico-Rei\", \"fortaleza-ce\", \"ceara-ce\"),\n    (\"Clássico dos Clássicos\", \"sport-pe\", \"santa cruz-pe\"),\n    (\"Clássico das Multidões\", \"sport-pe\", \"nautico-pe\"),\n]\n\nPOSITION_GROUPS: dict[str, set[str]] = {\n    \"goalkeeper\": {\"GK\"},\n    \"defender\": {\"CB\", \"LCB\", \"RCB\", \"LB\", \"RB\", \"LWB\", \"RWB\"},\n    \"midfielder\": {\"CM\", \"LCM\", \"RCM\", \"CDM\", \"LDM\", \"RDM\", \"CAM\", \"LAM\", \"RAM\", \"LM\", \"RM\"},\n    \"forward\": {\"ST\", \"LS\", \"RS\", \"CF\", \"LF\", \"RF\", \"LW\", \"RW\"},\n}\n\nALL_COMPETITIONS = [SERIE_A, SERIE_B, SERIE_C, COPA_DO_BRASIL, LIBERTADORES]\n\n\ndef match_competitions(query: str | None) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Translate a free-text competition name to canonical competition names.\"\"\"\n    if not query:\n        return list(ALL_COMPETITIONS)\n    needle = normalize_text(query)\n    for needles, canonical in COMPETITION_ALIASES:\n        if any(n in needle for n in needles):\n            return [canonical]\n    return []\n\n\nclass SoccerStore:\n    \"\"\"Repository of matches, players and teams with query helpers.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, data_dir: Path | str = \"data/kaggle\") -> None:\n        self.data_dir = Path(data_dir)\n        raw_matches, self.players, self.registry = load_all(self.data_dir)\n        self.matches, self.duplicate_count = self._deduplicate(raw_matches)\n        self._by_team: dict[str, list[int]] = defaultdict(list)\n        self._by_competition: dict[str, list[int]] = defaultdict(list)\n        for index, match in enumerate(self.matches):\n            self._by_team[match.home].append(index)\n            self._by_team[match.away].append(index)\n            self._by_competition[match.competition].append(index)\n        self._players_by_club: dict[str, list[Player]] = defaultdict(list)\n        for player in self.players:\n            if player.club:\n                club_id = self.registry.resolve(player.club)\n                if club_id:\n                    self._players_by_club[club_id].append(player)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _deduplicate(matches: list[Match]) -> tuple[list[Match], int]:\n        \"\"\"Merge matches shared across datasets, keeping the richest record.\n\n        Duplicates are identified by (date, home, away, competition); the\n        record from the highest-priority source is kept and enriched with any\n        fields (venue, stats, kick-off time) only present in the duplicate.\n        \"\"\"\n        seen: dict[tuple, int] = {}\n        result: list[Match] = []\n        duplicates = 0\n        for match in matches:\n            key = (match.date, match.home, match.away, match.competition)\n            if match.date is None:\n                result.append(match)\n                continue\n            if key not in seen:\n                seen[key] = len(result)\n                result.append(match)\n                continue\n            duplicates += 1\n            existing = result[seen[key]]\n            if SOURCE_PRIORITY[match.source] < SOURCE_PRIORITY[existing.source]:\n                match, existing = existing, match\n                result[seen[key]] = match\n            for field_name in (\n                \"venue\", \"time\", \"home_state\", \"away_state\", \"round\", \"stage\",\n                \"home_corners\", \"away_corners\", \"total_corners\", \"home_shots\",\n                \"away_shots\", \"home_attacks\", \"away_attacks\", \"ht_result\",\n                \"at_result\", \"season\",\n            ):\n                if getattr(match, field_name) is None and getattr(existing, field_name) is not None:\n                    setattr(match, field_name, getattr(existing, field_name))\n        return result, duplicates\n\n    def resolve_team(self, name: str) -> str | None:\n        return self.registry.resolve(name) if name else None\n\n    def team_display(self, cid: str) -> str:\n        return self.registry.display(cid)\n\n    def suggest_teams(self, query: str, limit: int = 8) -> list[str]:\n        return self.registry.suggest(query, limit)\n\n    def competitions_summary(self) -> list[dict]:\n        \"\"\"Per-competition coverage: seasons, match counts and team counts.\"\"\"\n        summary: dict[str, dict] = {}\n        for match in self.matches:\n            entry = summary.setdefault(\n                match.competition,\n                {\"competition\": match.competition, \"matches\": 0, \"seasons\": set(), \"teams\": set()},\n            )\n            entry[\"matches\"] += 1\n            if match.season:\n                entry[\"seasons\"].add(match.season)\n            entry[\"teams\"].add(match.home)\n            entry[\"teams\"].add(match.away)\n        rows = []\n        for competition in ALL_COMPETITIONS:\n            entry = summary.get(competition)\n            if not entry:\n                continue\n            rows.append(\n                {\n                    \"competition\": competition,\n                    \"matches\": entry[\"matches\"],\n                    \"seasons\": f\"{min(entry['seasons'])}-{max(entry['seasons'])}\" if entry[\"seasons\"] else \"n/a\",\n                    \"teams\": len(entry[\"teams\"]),\n                }\n            )\n        return rows\n\n    def find_matches(\n        self,\n        team: str | None = None,\n        opponent: str | None = None,\n        competition: str | None = None,\n        season: int | None = None,\n        date_from: str | date | None = None,\n        date_to: str | date | None = None,\n        stage: str | None = None,\n        venue: str = \"any\",\n        only_played: bool = False,\n        limit: int | None = 50,\n    ) -> tuple[list[Match], int]:\n        \"\"\"Find matches by team, opponent, competition, season, date or stage.\n\n        ``venue`` is 'any', 'home' or 'away' relative to ``team``. Returns the\n        (possibly truncated) match list plus the total number of matches that\n        matched the filters.\n        \"\"\"\n        team_id = self.resolve_team(team) if team else None\n        opponent_id = self.resolve_team(opponent) if opponent else None\n        if team and not team_id:\n            return [], 0\n        if opponent and not opponent_id:\n            return [], 0\n        competitions = match_competitions(competition)\n        if competition and not competitions:\n            return [], 0\n        from_date = _coerce_date(date_from)\n        to_date = _coerce_date(date_to)\n        stage_needle = normalize_text(stage) if stage else None\n\n        candidates: Iterable[int]\n        if team_id:\n            candidates = self._by_team.get(team_id, [])\n        else:\n            candidates = range(len(self.matches))\n\n        matched: list[Match] = []\n        for index in candidates:\n            match = self.matches[index]\n            if team_id and not match.involves(team_id):\n                continue\n            if team_id and venue == \"home\" and match.home != team_id:\n                continue\n            if team_id and venue == \"away\" and match.away != team_id:\n                continue\n            if opponent_id and not match.involves(opponent_id):\n                continue\n            if team_id and opponent_id and match.home == match.away:\n                continue\n            if competitions and match.competition not in competitions:\n                continue\n            if season is not None and match.season != season:\n                continue\n            if from_date and (match.date is None or match.date < from_date):\n                continue\n            if to_date and (match.date is None or match.date > to_date):\n                continue\n            if stage_needle:\n                haystack = normalize_text(f\"{match.stage or ''} {match.round or ''} r{match.round or ''}\")\n                if stage_needle not in haystack and f\"round {match.round}\" != f\"{stage}\":\n                    continue\n            if only_played and not match.played:\n                continue\n            matched.append(match)\n        matched.sort(key=lambda m: (m.date is None, m.date), reverse=True)\n        total = len(matched)\n        if limit is not None:\n            return matched[:limit], total\n        return matched, total\n\n    def head_to_head(\n        self, team_a: str, team_b: str, competition: str | None = None\n    ) -> dict | None:\n        \"\"\"Head-to-head record between two teams across the datasets.\"\"\"\n        a_id = self.resolve_team(team_a)\n        b_id = self.resolve_team(team_b)\n        if not a_id or not b_id:\n            return None\n        matches, _total = self.find_matches(\n            team=a_id, opponent=b_id, competition=competition, limit=None\n        )\n        a_record = TeamRecord(team=a_id, display=self.team_display(a_id))\n        b_record = TeamRecord(team=b_id, display=self.team_display(b_id))\n        for match in matches:\n            a_record.add(match)\n            b_record.add(match)\n        return {\n            \"team_a\": a_record.to_dict(),\n            \"team_b\": b_record.to_dict(),\n            \"matches\": matches,\n        }\n\n    def team_stats(\n        self,\n        team: str,\n        season: int | None = None,\n        competition: str | None = None,\n    ) -> dict | None:\n        \"\"\"Overall/home/away records plus per-competition and per-season splits.\"\"\"\n        team_id = self.resolve_team(team)\n        if not team_id:\n            return None\n        matches, _total = self.find_matches(\n            team=team_id, season=season, competition=competition, limit=None\n        )\n        overall = TeamRecord(team=team_id, display=self.team_display(team_id))\n        home = TeamRecord(team=team_id, display=self.team_display(team_id))\n        away = TeamRecord(team=team_id, display=self.team_display(team_id))\n        by_competition: dict[str, TeamRecord] = {}\n        by_season: dict[int, TeamRecord] = {}\n        for match in matches:\n            overall.add(match)\n            (home if match.home == team_id else away).add(match)\n            comp_record = by_competition.setdefault(\n                match.competition,\n                TeamRecord(team=team_id, display=self.team_display(team_id)),\n            )\n            comp_record.add(match)\n            if match.season:\n                season_record = by_season.setdefault(\n                    match.season,\n                    TeamRecord(team=team_id, display=self.team_display(team_id)),\n                )\n                season_record.add(match)\n        return {\n            \"team\": self.team_display(team_id),\n            \"canonical_id\": team_id,\n            \"overall\": overall.to_dict(),\n            \"home\": home.to_dict(),\n            \"away\": away.to_dict(),\n            \"by_competition\": [\n                by_competition[name].to_dict() for name in ALL_COMPETITIONS if name in by_competition\n            ],\n            \"by_season\": [\n                by_season[year].to_dict() for year in sorted(by_season, reverse=True)\n            ],\n        }\n\n    def standings(self, season: int, competition: str = SERIE_A) -> dict | None:\n        \"\"\"League table computed from match results for one season.\"\"\"\n        competitions = match_competitions(competition)\n        if not competitions:\n            return None\n        canonical = competitions[0]\n        if canonical == LIBERTADORES:\n            return self._libertadores_summary(season)\n        matches, _total = self.find_matches(\n            competition=canonical, season=season, limit=None, only_played=True\n        )\n        if not matches:\n            return None\n        records: dict[str, TeamRecord] = {}\n        for match in matches:\n            for team in (match.home, match.away):\n                if team not in records:\n                    records[team] = TeamRecord(team=team, display=match.home_display if team == match.home else match.away_display)\n            records[match.home].add(match)\n            records[match.away].add(match)\n        table = sorted(\n            records.values(),\n            key=lambda r: (-r.points, -r.wins, -r.goal_diff, -r.goals_for, r.display),\n        )\n        return {\n            \"season\": season,\n            \"competition\": canonical,\n            \"table\": [record.to_dict() for record in table],\n            \"champion\": table[0].to_dict() if table else None,\n            \"relegated\": [record.to_dict() for record in table[-4:]],\n        }\n\n    def _libertadores_summary(self, season: int) -> dict | None:\n        \"\"\"Stage-by-stage summary for a Libertadores season.\"\"\"\n        matches, _total = self.find_matches(\n            competition=LIBERTADORES, season=season, limit=None\n        )\n        if not matches:\n            return None\n        stages: dict[str, list[Match]] = defaultdict(list)\n        for match in matches:\n            stages[match.stage or \"unknown\"].append(match)\n        stage_summary = []\n        for stage_name in (\"group stage\", \"round of 16\", \"quarterfinals\", \"semifinals\", \"final\"):\n            if stage_name in stages:\n                stage_matches = sorted(stages[stage_name], key=lambda m: (m.date is None, m.date))\n                stage_summary.append(\n                    {\"stage\": stage_name, \"matches\": stage_matches}\n                )\n        return {\n            \"season\": season,\n            \"competition\": LIBERTADORES,\n            \"stages\": stage_summary,\n        }\n\n    def biggest_wins(\n        self,\n        competition: str | None = None,\n        season: int | None = None,\n        limit: int = 10,\n    ) -> list[Match]:\n        \"\"\"Largest goal-margin victories, newest first.\"\"\"\n        matches, _total = self.find_matches(\n            competition=competition, season=season, limit=None, only_played=True\n        )\n        ranked = sorted(\n            matches,\n            key=lambda m: (-(m.margin or 0), -(m.goals or 0), m.date is None, m.date),\n        )\n        return ranked[:limit]\n\n    def goals_analysis(\n        self, competition: str | None = None, season: int | None = None\n    ) -> dict | None:\n        \"\"\"Average goals, home/away win rates and draw rate for a filter set.\"\"\"\n        matches, _total = self.find_matches(\n            competition=competition, season=season, limit=None, only_played=True\n        )\n        if not matches:\n            return None\n        played = [m for m in matches if m.played]\n        total_goals = sum(m.goals or 0 for m in played)\n        home_wins = sum(1 for m in played if m.home_goals > m.away_goals)\n        away_wins = sum(1 for m in played if m.home_goals < m.away_goals)\n        draws = len(played) - home_wins - away_wins\n        count = len(played)\n        return {\n            \"matches\": count,\n            \"total_goals\": total_goals,\n            \"avg_goals_per_match\": round(total_goals / count, 2) if count else 0,\n            \"avg_home_goals\": round(sum(m.home_goals for m in played) / count, 2) if count else 0,\n            \"avg_away_goals\": round(sum(m.away_goals for m in played) / count, 2) if count else 0,\n            \"home_win_rate\": round(100 * home_wins / count, 1) if count else 0,\n            \"away_win_rate\": round(100 * away_wins / count, 1) if count else 0,\n            \"draw_rate\": round(100 * draws / count, 1) if count else 0,\n        }\n\n    def best_records(\n        self,\n        competition: str | None = None,\n        season: int | None = None,\n        venue: str = \"overall\",\n        min_matches: int = 10,\n        limit: int = 10,\n    ) -> list[dict]:\n        \"\"\"Rank teams by points-per-game for a filter set and venue.\"\"\"\n        matches, _total = self.find_matches(\n            competition=competition, season=season, limit=None, only_played=True\n        )\n        records: dict[str, TeamRecord] = {}\n        for match in matches:\n            teams = ((match.home,) if venue == \"home\" else (match.away,) if venue == \"away\" else (match.home, match.away))\n            for team in teams:\n                record = records.setdefault(\n                    team, TeamRecord(team=team, display=self.team_display(team))\n                )\n                record.add(match)\n        eligible = [r for r in records.values() if r.matches >= min_matches]\n        eligible.sort(key=lambda r: (-r.points / r.matches, -r.win_rate, -r.goal_diff, r.display))\n        return [record.to_dict() | {\"ppg\": round(record.points / record.matches, 2)} for record in eligible[:limit]]\n\n    def derbies(\n        self,\n        season: int | None = None,\n        competition: str | None = None,\n        limit: int = 50,\n    ) -> dict[str, list[Match]]:\n        \"\"\"Matches between traditional rival pairs (famous Brazilian derbies).\"\"\"\n        result: dict[str, list[Match]] = defaultdict(list)\n        for name, team_a, team_b in DERBIES:\n            if not self.registry.is_known(team_a) or not self.registry.is_known(team_b):\n                continue\n            matches, _total = self.find_matches(\n                team=team_a,\n                opponent=team_b,\n                season=season,\n                competition=competition,\n                limit=limit,\n            )\n            if matches:\n                result[name] = matches\n        return dict(result)\n\n    def player_search(\n        self,\n        name: str | None = None,\n        nationality: str | None = None,\n        club: str | None = None,\n        position: str | None = None,\n        min_overall: int | None = None,\n        max_overall: int | None = None,\n        max_age: int | None = None,\n        order_by: str = \"overall\",\n        limit: int = 20,\n    ) -> tuple[list[Player], int]:\n        \"\"\"Search FIFA players by name, nationality, club, position or ratings.\n\n        ``club`` accepts Brazilian team names in any spelling (e.g.\n        'Athletico-PR', 'Atlético Paranaense') as well as raw club names.\n        \"\"\"\n        name_needle = normalize_text(name) if name else None\n        nationality_needle = normalize_text(nationality) if nationality else None\n        club_ids = None\n        if club:\n            club_ids = {self.resolve_team(club)} if self.resolve_team(club) else set()\n            raw_needle = normalize_text(club)\n            for player in self.players:\n                if player.club and raw_needle and raw_needle in normalize_text(player.club):\n                    resolved = self.resolve_team(player.club)\n                    if resolved:\n                        club_ids.add(resolved)\n            if not club_ids:\n                return [], 0\n        positions = self._expand_positions(position)\n        matched: list[Player] = []\n        for player in self.players:\n            if name_needle and name_needle not in normalize_text(player.name):\n                continue\n            if nationality_needle and nationality_needle not in normalize_text(player.nationality):\n                continue\n            if club_ids is not None:\n                player_club = self.resolve_team(player.club) if player.club else None\n                if player_club not in club_ids:\n                    continue\n            if positions is not None and player.position not in positions:\n                continue\n            if min_overall is not None and (player.overall is None or player.overall < min_overall):\n                continue\n            if max_overall is not None and (player.overall is None or player.overall > max_overall):\n                continue\n            if max_age is not None and (player.age is None or player.age > max_age):\n                continue\n            matched.append(player)\n        sort_key = _player_sort_key(order_by)\n        reverse = order_by.lower() in {\"overall\", \"potential\", \"age\", \"value\"}\n        matched.sort(key=sort_key, reverse=reverse)\n        total = len(matched)\n        return matched[:limit], total\n\n    def _expand_positions(self, position: str | None) -> set[str] | None:\n        if not position:\n            return None\n        needle = normalize_text(position)\n        if needle in POSITION_GROUPS:\n            return POSITION_GROUPS[needle]\n        shortened = {\"gk\": \"goalkeeper\", \"gol\": \"goalkeeper\", \"goleiro\": \"goalkeeper\"}\n        if needle in shortened:\n            return POSITION_GROUPS[shortened[needle]]\n        compact = needle.replace(\" \", \"\")\n        for group, codes in POSITION_GROUPS.items():\n            if compact == normalize_text(group).replace(\" \", \"\"):\n                return codes\n        return {position.upper()}\n\n    def brazilian_clubs_with_squads(self) -> list[dict]:\n        \"\"\"FIFA clubs that correspond to Brazilian teams in the match data.\"\"\"\n        clubs = []\n        for club_id, players in self._players_by_club.items():\n            if not self.registry.is_known(club_id):\n                continue\n            base = club_id.rsplit(\"-\", 1)[0]\n            has_matches = any(\n                index in self._by_team.get(club_id, []) for index in (0,)\n            ) or bool(self._by_team.get(club_id))\n            if not has_matches:\n                continue\n            overalls = [p.overall for p in players if p.overall is not None]\n            clubs.append(\n                {\n                    \"club\": self.team_display(club_id),\n                    \"players\": len(players),\n                    \"avg_overall\": round(sum(overalls) / len(overalls), 1) if overalls else None,\n                }\n            )\n        clubs.sort(key=lambda c: (-c[\"players\"], c[\"club\"]))\n        return clubs\n\n    def squad_of(self, team: str) -> list[Player]:\n        \"\"\"All FIFA players whose club matches a Brazilian team name.\"\"\"\n        team_id = self.resolve_team(team)\n        if not team_id:\n            return []\n        return self._players_by_club.get(team_id, [])\n\n\ndef _coerce_date(value: str | date | None) -> date | None:\n    if value is None or isinstance(value, date):\n        return value\n    from .dates import parse_date\n\n    return parse_date(value)\n\n\ndef _player_sort_key(order_by: str):\n    field = order_by.lower().replace(\" \", \"_\")\n    aliases = {\n        \"rating\": \"overall\",\n        \"overall\": \"overall\",\n        \"potential\": \"potential\",\n        \"age\": \"age\",\n        \"name\": \"name\",\n        \"value\": \"value\",\n    }\n    field = aliases.get(field, \"overall\")\n\n    def key(player: Player):\n        value = getattr(player, field)\n        if field in {\"name\", \"value\"}:\n            return (value is None, str(value or \"\").lower())\n        return (value is None, value if value is not None else 0, player.name.lower())\n\n    return key\n\n\ndef default_data_dir() -> Path:\n    \"\"\"Locate the bundled data directory from CWD or the package parent.\"\"\"\n    candidates = [\n        Path.cwd() / \"data\" / \"kaggle\",\n        Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2].parent / \"data\" / \"kaggle\",\n        Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2] / \"data\" / \"kaggle\",\n    ]\n    for candidate in candidates:\n        if candidate.is_dir():\n            return candidate\n    return Path.cwd() / \"data\" / \"kaggle\"\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/store.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/store.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"src/brasil_mcp/store.py","time":{"start":1788227241864,"end":1788227241870}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait — there's an issue in `load_all`: the FIFA club observation happens AFTER match loading, so bare FIFA names like \"Santos\" would already be resolved during match loading (good), but the FIFA club observation adds canonical_raws for e.g. 'Santos' → but 'Santos' bare was already observed in match data. The issue: FIFA clubs like \"Atlético Mineiro\" need to resolve to atletico-mg. Since registry finalized before, but resolve() uses parse + DEFAULT_UF/aliases — 'atletico mineiro' is in TEAM_ALIASES → ('atletico','MG') → 'atletico-mg' ✓ regardless of observation order. 'Ceará Sporting Club' → alias ✓. 'América FC (Minas Gerais)' → parse: paren content 'minas gerais'... wait — my `_extract_country_tag` only extracts paren tags matching COUNTRY_CODES; '(Minas Gerais)' isn't. Then `_strip_parens` removes it → 'america fc' → filter 'fc' → 'america' → DEFAULT_UF['america']='MG' → america-mg ✓. Hmm wait, but I also had planned extracting state names from parens. Since DEFAULT_UF pins 'america'→MG, it works. But careful: 'América FC (Natal)' would also resolve to america-mg ✗ — but FIFA only has the MG one. And match data 'America FC Natal' → alias → RN ✓. OK.\n\nBut another subtlety: `_strip_parens` happens after `_extract_country_tag` — 'Nacional (URU)' → country URU ✓. 'Guaraní (PAR)' → PAR ✓.\n\nThere's a bug in `_team()` in loaders: convoluted fallback. `registry.resolve(raw)` returns None only if base unseen (after DEFAULT_UF + base_ufs check). If None, I observe the raw then re-resolve. But `_parse_fallback` + canonical_id construction is messy and could produce ids inconsistent with resolve(). Let me simplify: \n\n```python\ndef _team(registry, raw):\n    cid = registry.resolve(raw)\n    if cid is None:\n        registry.observe(raw)\n        cid = registry.resolve(raw) or parse fallback...\n    return cid, registry.display(cid)\n```\n\nActually since load_all pre-observes ALL names before loading, resolve() should never fail during match loading. The fallback is only for direct loader use without pre-observation. Keep it but simplify — drop the weird `_parse_fallback` dance:\n\n```python\ndef _team(registry, raw):\n    cid = registry.resolve(raw)\n    if cid is None:\n        registry.observe(raw)\n        cid = registry.resolve(raw)\n    if cid is None:\n        cid = raw.strip().lower()\n    return cid, registry.display(cid) if cid else raw\n```\n\nHmm, but display() for unknown cid falls back to cid.replace('-',' ').title(). If cid == raw.lower() (foreign name like 'boca juniors'), display 'Boca Juniors' ✓.\n\nWait, actually there IS a real issue: resolve() returns None when base not in _base_ufs AND no DEFAULT_UF pin AND no uf/country. E.g., 'Boca Juniors' — during pre-observation in load_all, registry.observe('Boca Juniors') records base_ufs['boca juniors'] = {'': count}. So resolve works during loading since pre-observed. ✓. For standalone loader use, _team observes on demand ✓.\n\nAnother issue: `_team` calls registry.observe but display comes from _displays which is only built in finalize(). If loaders are used standalone (tests), display(cid) returns fallback title-case — acceptable. In load_all flow, finalize() runs before loaders, so displays exist ✓. But when FIFA clubs are observed later and finalize called again — display recomputed ✓. However: display for teams observed ONLY in FIFA (e.g., 'Paris Saint-Germain' as club) — irrelevant for teams. For team_players I resolve club → canonical via registry.resolve(club) — 'Paris Saint-Germain' → base 'paris saint germain'... wait '-' → space → 'paris saint germain' base, no uf → in _base_ufs after observation ✓ → canonical 'paris saint germain'. Fine — players_at_club('Paris Saint-Germain') works.\n\nBut hmm: FIFA club 'Grêmio' → observe('Grêmio') → parse → base 'gremio' no uf → _canonical_id_for resolves via DEFAULT_UF['gremio']='RS' → 'gremio-rs' ✓ and _base_ufs['gremio'][''] += 1 — wait, that pollutes: _base_ufs['gremio'] would have {'RS': big, '': 1}. _resolve_uf checks distinct = {u for u in ufs if u} — filters out empty string ✓ good.\n\nOne more: `observe` adds to _base_ufs[base][(uf or country or '').upper()] — for country-tagged, base gets country code as pseudo-uf. For 'guarani': observations 'Guarani' (novo, no uf → ''), 'Guaraní (PAR)' → 'PAR', 'Guarani - SP' → 'SP'. distinct non-empty = {PAR, SP} → resolve('Guarani') bare → DEFAULT_UF['guarani']='SP' ✓ (pinned). \n\nWait, is 'guarani' in DEFAULT_UF? Yes I added it. ✓\n\nAlso 'atletico' base: observations 'Atletico-GO'→GO, 'Atletico-MG'→MG, 'Athletico-PR'→(fold)PR, 'Athletico' bare → ''. distinct={GO,MG,PR} → DEFAULT_UF['atletico']='PR' (Athletico-PR, the Libertadores regular). Hmm — but a user asking \"Atlético\" probably means MG more often... but in the data, bare 'Athletico' (libertadores NA row) = PR. Keep PR.\n\nWait, one more check on `_extract_uf`: `len(tokens[-1]) == 2 and tokens[-1].upper() in BRAZILIAN_UFS`. 'America MG' → tokens [america, mg] ✓ → MG. But 'Go' as in... 'Goiás GO' ✓. What about names like 'ABC'? single token, no. 'CRB'? 'CRB' is a club (Alagoas)! tokens=[crb] single → len>1 required → safe ✓. 'CSA' single ✓. But 'Bela Vista - RJ' fine. What about '4 de Julho EC'? tokens [4, de, julho, ec] → no 2-letter trailing ('ec' is 2 letters but not UF) ✓ → filter ec → '4 de julho' ✓.\n\nDanger: 'Vila Nova-GO' ✓ suffix. 'Interporto-TO'? fine. What about club 'Avaí' vs 'Avai-SC' → both → avai-sc? 'Avai' bare → DEFAULT_UF avai→SC → avai-sc ✓ merged.\n\n'Cuiaba-MT' & 'Cuiaba MT' → cuiaba-mt ✓. FIFA? no cuiaba club. ✓\n\n'Criciuma' bare + 'Criciuma-SC' → criciuma-sc ✓.\n\nNow — the Brasileirão 2023: brf only (377 matches). Palmeiras 2023 = 37 matches. Fine.\n\nNow store.py. Dedupe: key = (date, home, away, competition). Note brf date has no time; bras datetime → date. Same match same date ✓. But cuidado: Copa do Brasil two-legged ties — same teams, different dates ✓ no collision. Libertadores group stage home/away different dates ✓.\n\nEdge: could two DIFFERENT matches share (date, home, away, competition)? E.g., a match postponed & replayed same day? No. Replays in Copa do Brasil era? No. Safe.\n\nMerge: keep first (priority order of loading: brasileirao, copa, libertadores, historico, br_football — wait load order in load_all: bras, cup, lib, brf, novo. Priority by source: brasileirao(0), copa_do_brasil(1), libertadores(2), brasileirao_historico(3), br_football(4). When merging into existing, enrich existing with missing fields from the new one (venue, stats, time, states).\n\nNow write store.py with all query methods.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05aa64782001nenPnYbeGpQkjY","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05aa4b968001r40OD455esVVs2"}}
