{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788227387542,"sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_d0a34da9105743b3abf059f2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"In-memory knowledge store unifying all match and player datasets.\n\nThe store loads the six CSVs once, deduplicates matches that appear in more\nthan one dataset (the 2012-2019 Série A seasons exist in three files), builds\nteam/player indexes, and exposes the query surface used by the MCP tools and\nthe CLI.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom datetime import date\nfrom pathlib import re as _re_unused  # noqa: F401  (kept for lint parity)\n\nfrom .dates import parse_date\nfrom .loaders import (\n    COPA_DO_BRASIL,\n    LIBERTADORES,\n    SERIE_A,\n    SERIE_B,\n    SERIE_C,\n    load_all,\n)\nfrom .models import Match, Player, TeamRecord\nfrom .normalize import BRAZILIAN_UFS, TeamRegistry, normalize_text\n\nSOURCE_PRIORITY = {\n    \"brasileirao\": 0,\n    \"copa_do_brasil\": 1,\n    \"libertadores\": 2,\n    \"brasileiro_historico\": 3,\n    \"brasileirao_historico\": 3,\n    \"br_football\": 4,\n}\n\nCOMPETITION_ALIASES: list[tuple[tuple[str, ...], str]] = [\n    ((\"libertadores\",), LIBERTADORES),\n    ((\"copa do brasil\", \"copadobrasil\", \"cdb\", \"brazilian cup\"), COPA_DO_BRASIL),\n    ((\"serie b\", \"serieb\", \"b series\", \"serie b brasileirao\"), SERIE_B),\n    ((\"serie c\", \"seriec\", \"c series\"), SERIE_C),\n    ((\"serie a\", \"seriea\", \"brasileirao\", \"brasileirao serie a\"), SERIE_A),\n]\n\nDERBIES: list[tuple[str, str, str]] = [\n    (\"Fla-Flu\", \"flamengo-rj\", \"fluminense-rj\"),\n    (\"Clássico dos Milhões\", \"flamengo-rj\", \"vasco-rj\"),\n    (\"Clássico Vovô\", \"botafogo-rj\", \"fluminense-rj\"),\n    (\"Majestoso\", \"corinthians-sp\", \"sao paulo-sp\"),\n    (\"Choque-Rei\", \"palmeiras-sp\", \"sao paulo-sp\"),\n    (\"Derby Paulista\", \"palmeiras-sp\", \"corinthians-sp\"),\n    (\"Grenal\", \"gremio-rs\", \"internacional-rs\"),\n    (\"Atletiba\", \"atletico-pr\", \"coritiba-pr\"),\n    (\"Ba-Vi\", \"bahia-ba\", \"vitoria-ba\"),\n    (\"Clássico-Rei\", \"fortaleza-ce\", \"ceara-ce\"),\n    (\"Clássico dos Clássicos\", \"sport-pe\", \"santa cruz-pe\"),\n    (\"Clássico das Multidões\", \"sport-pe\", \"nautico-pe\"),\n]\n\nPOSITION_GROUPS: dict[str, set[str]] = {\n    \"goalkeeper\": {\"GK\"},\n    \"defender\": {\"CB\", \"LCB\", \"RCB\", \"LB\", \"RB\", \"LWB\", \"RWB\"},\n    \"midfielder\": {\"CM\", \"LCM\", \"RCM\", \"CDM\", \"LDM\", \"RDM\", \"CAM\", \"LAM\", \"RAM\", \"LM\", \"RM\"},\n    \"forward\": {\"ST\", \"LS\", \"RS\", \"CF\", \"LF\", \"RF\", \"LW\", \"RW\"},\n}\n\nFINAL_WORDS = {\"final\", \"finals\", \"finais\", \"decisao\", \"championship match\"}\n\nALL_COMPETITIONS = [SERIE_A, SERIE_B, SERIE_C, COPA_DO_BRASIL, LIBERTADORES]\n\n\ndef match_competitions(query: str | None) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Translate a free-text competition name to canonical competition names.\"\"\"\n    if not query:\n        return list(ALL_COMPETITIONS)\n    needle = normalize_text(query)\n    for needles, canonical in COMPETITION_ALIASES:\n        if any(n in needle for n in needles):\n            return [canonical]\n    return []\n\n\ndef _is_brazilian_club(club_id: str) -> bool:\n    parts = club_id.rsplit(\"-\", 1)\n    return len(parts) == 2 and parts[1].upper() in BRAZILIAN_UFS\n\n\nclass SoccerStore:\n    \"\"\"Repository of matches, players and teams with query helpers.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, data_dir: Path | str = \"data/kaggle\") -> None:\n        self.data_dir = Path(data_dir)\n        raw_matches, self.players, self.registry = load_all(self.data_dir)\n        self.matches, self.duplicate_count = self._deduplicate(raw_matches)\n        self._by_team: dict[str, list[int]] = defaultdict(list)\n        self._by_competition: dict[str, list[int]] = defaultdict(list)\n        for index, match in enumerate(self.matches):\n            self._by_team[match.home].append(index)\n            self._by_team[match.away].append(index)\n            self._by_competition[match.competition].append(index)\n        self._cup_final_rounds: dict[int, str] = {}\n        for match in self.matches:\n            if match.competition == COPA_DO_BRASIL and match.season is not None and match.round:\n                current = self._cup_final_rounds.get(match.season)\n                try:\n                    round_num = int(match.round)\n                except ValueError:\n                    continue\n                current_num = int(current) if current else -1\n                if round_num > current_num:\n                    self._cup_final_rounds[match.season] = match.round\n        self._players_by_club: dict[str, list[Player]] = defaultdict(list)\n        for player in self.players:\n            if player.club:\n                club_id = self.registry.resolve(player.club)\n                if club_id:\n                    self._players_by_club[club_id].append(player)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _deduplicate(matches: list[Match]) -> tuple[list[Match], int]:\n        \"\"\"Merge matches shared across datasets, keeping the richest record.\n\n        Duplicates are identified by (date, home, away, competition); the\n        record from the highest-priority source is kept and enriched with any\n        fields (venue, stats, kick-off time) only present in the duplicate.\n        \"\"\"\n        seen: dict[tuple, int] = {}\n        result: list[Match] = []\n        duplicates = 0\n        for match in matches:\n            if match.date is None:\n                result.append(match)\n                continue\n            key = (match.date, match.home, match.away, match.competition)\n            if key not in seen:\n                seen[key] = len(result)\n                result.append(match)\n                continue\n            duplicates += 1\n            keeper_index = seen[key]\n            keeper = result[keeper_index]\n            other = match\n            if SOURCE_PRIORITY[other.source] < SOURCE_PRIORITY[keeper.source]:\n                keeper, other = other, keeper\n                result[keeper_index] = keeper\n            for field_name in (\n                \"venue\", \"time\", \"home_state\", \"away_state\", \"round\", \"stage\",\n                \"home_corners\", \"away_corners\", \"total_corners\", \"home_shots\",\n                \"away_shots\", \"home_attacks\", \"away_attacks\", \"ht_result\",\n                \"at_result\", \"season\",\n            ):\n                if getattr(keeper, field_name) is None and getattr(other, field_name) is not None:\n                    setattr(keeper, field_name, getattr(other, field_name))\n        return result, duplicates\n\n    def resolve_team(self, name: str | None) -> str | None:\n        return self.registry.resolve(name) if name else None\n\n    def team_display(self, cid: str) -> str:\n        return self.registry.display(cid)\n\n    def suggest_teams(self, query: str, limit: int = 8) -> list[str]:\n        return self.registry.suggest(query, limit)\n\n    def competitions_summary(self) -> list[dict]:\n        \"\"\"Per-competition coverage: seasons, match counts and team counts.\"\"\"\n        summary: dict[str, dict] = {}\n        for match in self.matches:\n            entry = summary.setdefault(\n                match.competition,\n                {\"competition\": match.competition, \"matches\": 0, \"seasons\": set(), \"teams\": set()},\n            )\n            entry[\"matches\"] += 1\n            if match.season:\n                entry[\"seasons\"].add(match.season)\n            entry[\"teams\"].add(match.home)\n            entry[\"teams\"].add(match.away)\n        rows = []\n        for competition in ALL_COMPETITIONS:\n            entry = summary.get(competition)\n            if not entry:\n                continue\n            rows.append(\n                {\n                    \"competition\": competition,\n                    \"matches\": entry[\"matches\"],\n                    \"seasons\": (\n                        f\"{min(entry['seasons'])}-{max(entry['seasons'])}\"\n                        if entry[\"seasons\"] else \"n/a\"\n                    ),\n                    \"teams\": len(entry[\"teams\"]),\n                }\n            )\n        return rows\n\n    def find_matches(\n        self,\n        team: str | None = None,\n        opponent: str | None = None,\n        competition: str | None = None,\n        season: int | None = None,\n        date_from: str | date | None = None,\n        date_to: str | date | None = None,\n        stage: str | None = None,\n        venue: str = \"any\",\n        only_played: bool = False,\n        limit: int | None = 50,\n    ) -> tuple[list[Match], int]:\n        \"\"\"Find matches by team, opponent, competition, season, date or stage.\n\n        ``venue`` is 'any', 'home' or 'away' relative to ``team``. Returns the\n        (possibly truncated) match list plus the total matching count.\n        \"\"\"\n        team_id = self.resolve_team(team) if team else None\n        opponent_id = self.resolve_team(opponent) if opponent else None\n        if team and not team_id:\n            return [], 0\n        if opponent and not opponent_id:\n            return [], 0\n        competitions = match_competitions(competition)\n        if competition and not competitions:\n            return [], 0\n        from_date = _coerce_date(date_from)\n        to_date = _coerce_date(date_to)\n\n        if team_id:\n            candidates: list[int] = list(self._by_team.get(team_id, []))\n        else:\n            candidates = list(range(len(self.matches)))\n\n        matched: list[Match] = []\n        for index in candidates:\n            match = self.matches[index]\n            if team_id and not match.involves(team_id):\n                continue\n            if team_id and venue == \"home\" and match.home != team_id:\n                continue\n            if team_id and venue == \"away\" and match.away != team_id:\n                continue\n            if opponent_id and not match.involves(opponent_id):\n                continue\n            if competitions and match.competition not in competitions:\n                continue\n            if season is not None and match.season != season:\n                continue\n            if from_date and (match.date is None or match.date < from_date):\n                continue\n            if to_date and (match.date is None or match.date > to_date):\n                continue\n            if stage and not self._stage_matches(match, stage):\n                continue\n            if only_played and not match.played:\n                continue\n            matched.append(match)\n        matched.sort(key=lambda m: (m.date is None, m.date or date.min), reverse=True)\n        total = len(matched)\n        return (matched[:limit], total) if limit is not None else (matched, total)\n\n    def _stage_matches(self, match: Match, stage: str) -> bool:\n        needle = normalize_text(stage)\n        if not needle:\n            return True\n        if needle in FINAL_WORDS:\n            if match.competition == COPA_DO_BRASIL:\n                return match.round == self._cup_final_rounds.get(match.season)\n            if match.competition == LIBERTADORES:\n                return (match.stage or \"\") == \"final\"\n        stage_text = normalize_text(match.stage or \"\")\n        if stage_text and (stage_text == needle or stage_text.startswith(needle)):\n            return True\n        round_text = normalize_text(match.round or \"\")\n        if round_text:\n            if round_text == needle or f\"round {round_text}\" == needle:\n                return True\n            if needle.isdigit() and round_text == needle:\n                return True\n        if needle.isdigit() and (match.round or \"\") == needle:\n            return True\n        return False\n\n    def head_to_head(\n        self, team_a: str, team_b: str, competition: str | None = None\n    ) -> dict | None:\n        \"\"\"Head-to-head record between two teams across the datasets.\"\"\"\n        a_id = self.resolve_team(team_a)\n        b_id = self.resolve_team(team_b)\n        if not a_id or not b_id:\n            return None\n        matches, _total = self.find_matches(\n            team=a_id, opponent=b_id, competition=competition, limit=None\n        )\n        a_record = TeamRecord(team=a_id, display=self.team_display(a_id))\n        b_record = TeamRecord(team=b_id, display=self.team_display(b_id))\n        for match in matches:\n            a_record.add(match)\n            b_record.add(match)\n        return {\n            \"team_a\": a_record.to_dict(),\n            \"team_b\": b_record.to_dict(),\n            \"matches\": matches,\n        }\n\n    def team_stats(\n        self,\n        team: str,\n        season: int | None = None,\n        competition: str | None = None,\n    ) -> dict | None:\n        \"\"\"Overall/home/away records plus per-competition and per-season splits.\"\"\"\n        team_id = self.resolve_team(team)\n        if not team_id:\n            return None\n        matches, _total = self.find_matches(\n            team=team_id, season=season, competition=competition, limit=None\n        )\n        display = self.team_display(team_id)\n        overall = TeamRecord(team=team_id, display=display)\n        home = TeamRecord(team=team_id, display=display)\n        away = TeamRecord(team=team_id, display=display)\n        by_competition: dict[str, TeamRecord] = {}\n        by_season: dict[int, TeamRecord] = {}\n        for match in matches:\n            overall.add(match)\n            (home if match.home == team_id else away).add(match)\n            comp_record = by_competition.setdefault(\n                match.competition, TeamRecord(team=team_id, display=display)\n            )\n            comp_record.add(match)\n            if match.season:\n                season_record = by_season.setdefault(\n                    match.season, TeamRecord(team=team_id, display=display)\n                )\n                season_record.add(match)\n        return {\n            \"team\": display,\n            \"canonical_id\": team_id,\n            \"overall\": overall.to_dict(),\n            \"home\": home.to_dict(),\n            \"away\": away.to_dict(),\n            \"by_competition\": [\n                by_competition[name].to_dict()\n                for name in ALL_COMPETITIONS\n                if name in by_competition\n            ],\n            \"by_season\": [\n                by_season[year].to_dict() for year in sorted(by_season, reverse=True)\n            ],\n        }\n\n    def standings(self, season: int, competition: str = SERIE_A) -> dict | None:\n        \"\"\"League table computed from match results for one season.\"\"\"\n        competitions = match_competitions(competition)\n        if not competitions:\n            return None\n        canonical = competitions[0]\n        if canonical == LIBERTADORES:\n            return self._libertadores_summary(season)\n        matches, _total = self.find_matches(\n            competition=canonical, season=season, limit=None, only_played=True\n        )\n        if not matches:\n            return None\n        records: dict[str, TeamRecord] = {}\n        for match in matches:\n            for team, display in (\n                (match.home, match.home_display),\n                (match.away, match.away_display),\n            ):\n                if team not in records:\n                    records[team] = TeamRecord(team=team, display=display)\n            records[match.home].add(match)\n            records[match.away].add(match)\n        table = sorted(\n            records.values(),\n            key=lambda r: (-r.points, -r.wins, -r.goal_diff, -r.goals_for, r.display),\n        )\n        return {\n            \"season\": season,\n            \"competition\": canonical,\n            \"table\": [record.to_dict() for record in table],\n            \"champion\": table[0].to_dict() if table else None,\n            \"relegated\": [record.to_dict() for record in table[-4:]],\n        }\n\n    def _libertadores_summary(self, season: int) -> dict | None:\n        \"\"\"Stage-by-stage summary for a Libertadores season.\"\"\"\n        matches, _total = self.find_matches(\n            competition=LIBERTADORES, season=season, limit=None\n        )\n        if not matches:\n            return None\n        stages: dict[str, list[Match]] = defaultdict(list)\n        for match in matches:\n            stages[match.stage or \"unknown\"].append(match)\n        stage_summary = []\n        for stage_name in (\"group stage\", \"round of 16\", \"quarterfinals\", \"semifinals\", \"final\"):\n            if stage_name in stages:\n                stage_matches = sorted(\n                    stages[stage_name], key=lambda m: (m.date is None, m.date or date.min)\n                )\n                stage_summary.append({\"stage\": stage_name, \"matches\": stage_matches})\n        return {\"season\": season, \"competition\": LIBERTADORES, \"stages\": stage_summary}\n\n    def biggest_wins(\n        self,\n        competition: str | None = None,\n        season: int | None = None,\n        limit: int = 10,\n    ) -> list[Match]:\n        \"\"\"Largest goal-margin victories, newest first among equal margins.\"\"\"\n        matches, _total = self.find_matches(\n            competition=competition, season=season, limit=None, only_played=True\n        )\n        ranked = sorted(\n            matches,\n            key=lambda m: (\n                -(m.margin or 0),\n                -(m.goals or 0),\n                m.date is None,\n                m.date or date.min,\n            ),\n        )\n        return ranked[:limit]\n\n    def goals_analysis(\n        self, competition: str | None = None, season: int | None = None\n    ) -> dict | None:\n        \"\"\"Average goals, home/away win rates and draw rate for a filter set.\"\"\"\n        matches, _total = self.find_matches(\n            competition=competition, season=season, limit=None, only_played=True\n        )\n        played = [m for m in matches if m.played]\n        if not played:\n            return None\n        count = len(played)\n        total_goals = sum(m.goals or 0 for m in played)\n        home_wins = sum(1 for m in played if m.home_goals > m.away_goals)\n        away_wins = sum(1 for m in played if m.home_goals < m.away_goals)\n        draws = count - home_wins - away_wins\n        return {\n            \"matches\": count,\n            \"total_goals\": total_goals,\n            \"avg_goals_per_match\": round(total_goals / count, 2),\n            \"avg_home_goals\": round(sum(m.home_goals for m in played) / count, 2),\n            \"avg_away_goals\": round(sum(m.away_goals for m in played) / count, 2),\n            \"home_win_rate\": round(100 * home_wins / count, 1),\n            \"away_win_rate\": round(100 * away_wins / count, 1),\n            \"draw_rate\": round(100 * draws / count, 1),\n        }\n\n    def best_records(\n        self,\n        competition: str | None = None,\n        season: int | None = None,\n        venue: str = \"overall\",\n        min_matches: int = 10,\n        limit: int = 10,\n    ) -> list[dict]:\n        \"\"\"Rank teams by points-per-game for a filter set and venue.\"\"\"\n        matches, _total = self.find_matches(\n            competition=competition, season=season, limit=None, only_played=True\n        )\n        records: dict[str, TeamRecord] = {}\n        for match in matches:\n            if venue == \"home\":\n                teams = (match.home,)\n            elif venue == \"away\":\n                teams = (match.away,)\n            else:\n                teams = (match.home, match.away)\n            for team in teams:\n                record = records.setdefault(\n                    team, TeamRecord(team=team, display=self.team_display(team))\n                )\n                record.add(match)\n        eligible = [r for r in records.values() if r.matches >= min_matches]\n        eligible.sort(key=lambda r: (-r.points / r.matches, -r.win_rate, -r.goal_diff, r.display))\n        return [\n            record.to_dict() | {\"ppg\": round(record.points / record.matches, 2)}\n            for record in eligible[:limit]\n        ]\n\n    def derbies(\n        self,\n        season: int | None = None,\n        competition: str | None = None,\n        limit: int = 50,\n    ) -> dict[str, list[Match]]:\n        \"\"\"Matches between traditional rival pairs (famous Brazilian derbies).\"\"\"\n        result: dict[str, list[Match]] = {}\n        for name, team_a, team_b in DERBIES:\n            if not self.registry.is_known(team_a) or not self.registry.is_known(team_b):\n                continue\n            matches, _total = self.find_matches(\n                team=team_a,\n                opponent=team_b,\n                season=season,\n                competition=competition,\n                limit=limit,\n            )\n            if matches:\n                result[name] = matches\n        return result\n\n    def player_search(\n        self,\n        name: str | None = None,\n        nationality: str | None = None,\n        club: str | None = None,\n        position: str | None = None,\n        min_overall: int | None = None,\n        max_overall: int | None = None,\n        max_age: int | None = None,\n        order_by: str = \"overall\",\n        limit: int = 20,\n    ) -> tuple[list[Player], int]:\n        \"\"\"Search FIFA players by name, nationality, club, position or ratings.\n\n        ``club`` accepts Brazilian team names in any spelling (e.g.\n        'Athletico-PR', 'Atlético Paranaense') as well as foreign club names.\n        \"\"\"\n        name_needle = normalize_text(name) if name else None\n        nationality_needle = normalize_text(nationality) if nationality else None\n        club_ids = self._resolve_club_filter(club)\n        if club and not club_ids:\n            return [], 0\n        positions = self._expand_positions(position)\n        matched: list[Player] = []\n        for player in self.players:\n            if name_needle and name_needle not in normalize_text(player.name):\n                continue\n            if nationality_needle and nationality_needle not in normalize_text(player.nationality):\n                continue\n            if club_ids is not None:\n                player_club = self.registry.resolve(player.club) if player.club else None\n                if player_club not in club_ids:\n                    continue\n            if positions is not None and player.position not in positions:\n                continue\n            if min_overall is not None and (player.overall is None or player.overall < min_overall):\n                continue\n            if max_overall is not None and (player.overall is None or player.overall > max_overall):\n                continue\n            if max_age is not None and (player.age is None or player.age > max_age):\n                continue\n            matched.append(player)\n        matched.sort(key=_player_sort_key(order_by), reverse=_sort_descending(order_by))\n        total = len(matched)\n        return matched[:limit], total\n\n    def _resolve_club_filter(self, club: str | None) -> set[str] | None:\n        \"\"\"Resolve a club query to the set of acceptable canonical club ids.\"\"\"\n        if not club:\n            return None\n        resolved = self.registry.resolve(club)\n        if resolved:\n            return {resolved}\n        needle = normalize_text(club)\n        if not needle:\n            return set()\n        matches_found = {\n            self.registry.resolve(player.club)\n            for player in self.players\n            if player.club and needle in normalize_text(player.club)\n        }\n        return {club_id for club_id in matches_found if club_id}\n\n    def _expand_positions(self, position: str | None) -> set[str] | None:\n        if not position:\n            return None\n        needle = normalize_text(position)\n        direct = {\"gk\": \"goalkeeper\", \"gol\": \"goalkeeper\", \"goleiro\": \"goalkeeper\"}\n        needle = direct.get(needle, needle)\n        if needle in POSITION_GROUPS:\n            return POSITION_GROUPS[needle]\n        if needle in {\"atacante\", \"striker\"}:\n            return POSITION_GROUPS[\"forward\"]\n        if needle in {\"meia\", \"meio campista\"}:\n            return POSITION_GROUPS[\"midfielder\"]\n        if needle in {\"zagueiro\", \"lateral\"}:\n            return POSITION_GROUPS[\"defender\"]\n        return {position.upper()}\n\n    def brazilian_clubs_with_squads(self) -> list[dict]:\n        \"\"\"FIFA clubs that correspond to Brazilian teams in the match data.\"\"\"\n        clubs = []\n        for club_id, players in self._players_by_club.items():\n            if not _is_brazilian_club(club_id):\n                continue\n            if not self._by_team.get(club_id):\n                continue\n            overalls = [p.overall for p in players if p.overall is not None]\n            clubs.append(\n                {\n                    \"club\": self.team_display(club_id),\n                    \"canonical_id\": club_id,\n                    \"players\": len(players),\n                    \"avg_overall\": round(sum(overalls) / len(overalls), 1) if overalls else None,\n                }\n            )\n        clubs.sort(key=lambda c: (-c[\"players\"], c[\"club\"]))\n        return clubs\n\n    def squad_of(self, team: str) -> list[Player]:\n        \"\"\"All FIFA players whose club matches a Brazilian team name.\"\"\"\n        team_id = self.resolve_team(team)\n        if not team_id:\n            return []\n        return self._players_by_club.get(team_id, [])\n\n\ndef _coerce_date(value: str | date | None) -> date | None:\n    if value is None or isinstance(value, date):\n        return value\n    return parse_date(value)\n\n\ndef _player_sort_key(order_by: str):\n    field = normalize_text(order_by).replace(\" \", \"_\")\n    field = {\"rating\": \"overall\"}.get(field, field)\n    if field not in {\"overall\", \"potential\", \"age\", \"name\", \"jersey\"}:\n        field = \"overall\"\n\n    def key(player: Player):\n        value = getattr(player, field)\n        if field == \"name\":\n            return value.lower()\n        if value is None:\n            return (1, 0, player.name.lower())\n        return (0, value, player.name.lower())\n\n    return key\n\n\ndef _sort_descending(order_by: str) -> bool:\n    field = normalize_text(order_by).replace(\" \", \"_\")\n    return field != \"name\"\n\n\ndef default_data_dir() -> Path:\n    \"\"\"Locate the bundled data directory from CWD or the package parents.\"\"\"\n    candidates = [\n        Path.cwd() / \"data\" / \"kaggle\",\n        Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2] / \"data\" / \"kaggle\",\n        Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3] / \"data\" / \"kaggle\",\n    ]\n    for candidate in candidates:\n        if candidate.is_dir():\n            return candidate\n    return Path.cwd() / \"data\" / \"kaggle\"\n\n\ndef is_valid_position(position: str) -> bool:\n    return bool(re.fullmatch(r\"[A-Z]{1,3}\", position.upper() or \"\"))\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/store.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/store.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"src/brasil_mcp/store.py","time":{"start":1788227387522,"end":1788227387540}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I need to fix a leftover ugly piece in `brazilian_clubs_with_squads` — the `has_matches` computation is convoluted. Simplify: `has_matches = bool(self._by_team.get(club_id))`.\n\nAlso there's a bug: in `find_matches`, the stage filter has weird logic `f\"round {match.round}\" != f\"{stage}\"` — let me clean that up. Stage matching should be: normalize stage query, check against match.stage and \"round N\" patterns. If user asks \"final\", match.stage contains 'final' ✓ (Libertadores final). If user asks \"round 22\" or \"22\", check round == '22' or stage contains. Let me rewrite:\n\n```python\nif stage_needle:\n    stage_text = normalize_text(match.stage or \"\")\n    round_text = normalize_text(f\"round {match.round}\" if match.round else \"\")\n    if stage_needle not in stage_text and stage_needle not in round_text and stage_needle != normalize_text(match.round or \"\"):\n        continue\n```\n\nAlso in `standings` — TeamRecord creation for home/away display: I wrote a hacky conditional. Cleaner:\n\n```python\nfor match in matches:\n    for team, display in ((match.home, match.home_display), (match.away, match.away_display)):\n        if team not in records:\n            records[team] = TeamRecord(team=team, display=display)\n```\n\nAlso `best_records`: `record.to_dict() | {\"ppg\": ...}` — dict union OK in 3.9+. Fine.\n\nAlso in `find_matches` there's a subtle issue with `venue` param: if `team_id` is None but venue specified — ignore. OK as documented (venue relative to team).\n\nAnd the `stage` filter's round match: `normalize_text(match.round or \"\")` — if stage query '22', round '22' matches ✓. If stage 'final' — Libertadores stage 'final' ✓. Copa do Brasil finals: rounds are numeric; \"final\" query won't match. For Copa do Brasil finals I should map: final = last round of season (round 8? hmm, actually the max round per season varies: 2012 had 8 rounds? earlier I saw rounds 1-8 with round 8 = 14 matches total across seasons — round 8 appears 14 times?? That means round 8 has 14 matches across multiple seasons — finals are 2 legs per season; if round 8 = final round in seasons 2012-2018 that's 7 seasons × 2 = 14 ✓!). So Copa do Brasil: round 7 = semifinal, round 8 = final (2 legs). I'll add special handling: when competition is Copa do Brasil and stage query mentions 'final', match the max round for that season. Simpler: in the queries layer (search_matches tool), for Copa do Brasil \"final\" queries, compute per-season max round. Hmm — complexity. Alternative: at load time for copa_do_brasil, annotate round names: map numeric round to stage labels? The Kaggle dataset docs don't define round numbers. Observed: rounds 1-8; final round per season = max round in that season. I'll implement stage filter with a helper: if needle contains 'final' → for cup matches, compute per-season max round and match those. Let me implement inside store.find_matches? That requires per-season max-round map for Copa do Brasil precomputed. I'll precompute `self._cup_final_rounds: dict[season, round]` at init, and handle in stage filter: if stage_needle in {'final','finais','finals'} and match.competition == COPA_DO_BRASIL: matched if match.round == self._cup_final_rounds.get(match.season). Also Libertadores 'final' stage matches via stage text ✓.\n\nActually wait — also 'semifinal' for cup (round 7) and 'quarterfinal'? Rounds structure: R1 (first round), R2 (second round), R3 (third round), R4 (round of 16), R5 (quarterfinals)? Hmm — 2012-2021 format varied (some seasons 7 rounds, some 8). Max round per season is reliably \"the final\". For semifinals, second-to-last round. I'll support 'final' only via this special case, and leave generic round matching for others. Good enough for \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\".\n\nLet me also double check `player_search` club matching: `club_ids = {self.resolve_team(club)} if self.resolve_team(club) else set()` — then adds raw-needle containment matches over ALL players' clubs (e.g., query 'Paris' would match 'Paris Saint-Germain', 'Paris FC'). This means query 'Santos' → resolve_team('Santos') → 'santos-sp'; containment: 'santos' in 'santos laguna' → resolve 'santos laguna' → adds 'santos laguna' → Mexican club would match! Bug. Fix: containment should only add clubs whose resolved canonical equals... no wait, the containment is meant to catch club names the registry doesn't know as teams (foreign clubs, e.g. query 'Paris Saint-Germain' → resolve_team returns None (not observed as team? it IS observed as FIFA club during load_all — I observe player clubs into registry! So 'Paris Saint-Germain' resolves via registry ✓). So registry already knows all FIFA clubs. Then resolve_team('Santos') → 'santos-sp' and 'santos laguna' is a different canonical → NOT matched ✓ without containment. The containment path is only needed when resolve fails entirely. So: club_ids = {resolve(club)} if resolved else {resolve(p.club) for players where needle in club name}. That keeps 'Santos' precise. \n\nEdge: user queries 'PSG' — not resolvable, no containment match → empty + suggestions. Fine.\n\nAnother subtlety: resolve_team('Santos') → DEFAULT_UF 'SP' → 'santos-sp'. Player club 'Santos' resolves to 'santos-sp' ✓. Player 'Santos Laguna' → parse: base 'santos laguna' no uf → _resolve_uf: distinct for base 'santos laguna' = {'': n} → filtered empty → distinct empty → len!=1 → returns None → base in _base_ufs → canonical 'santos laguna' ✓ different from santos-sp ✓.\n\nBut WAIT: DEFAULT_UF['santos']='SP' — resolve('Santos Laguna') calls parse_team_name → base 'santos laguna' → then `_resolve_uf('santos laguna')` → DEFAULT_UF.get('santos laguna') → None ✓ → distinct check on base_ufs['santos laguna']... contains only '' → filtered → empty set → returns None → falls to `if base in self._base_ufs: return base` → 'santos laguna' ✓.\n\nHmm, but one more: `_resolve_uf` with distinct empty returns None — good.\n\nWhat about 'Goiás' resolve → DEFAULT_UF goias → GO → 'goias-go'. Player club 'Goiás EC'? not in FIFA list shown... fine either way (alias).\n\nAlso 'Bahia' → DEFAULT_UF BA ✓. 'Vitória' → BA ✓. 'Botafogo' → RJ ✓ (Botafogo-PB exists in data as 'Botafogo-PB' → base botafogo ufs {RJ, PB} → DEFAULT pins RJ ✓).\n\n'Internacional' → RS ✓, 'Grêmio' → RS ✓, 'Cruzeiro' → MG ✓, 'Coritiba' → PR ✓, 'Paraná' → PR ✓, 'Ceará' → CE ✓, 'Fortaleza' → CE ✓, 'Chapecoense' → SC ✓, 'Sport' → PE ✓, 'América' → MG ✓, 'Atlético Mineiro' → alias MG ✓, 'Atlético Paranaense' → alias PR ✓, 'América FC (Minas Gerais)' → parse: alias? alias_key after stripping non-alnum: 'america fc minas gerais' — wait, parse_team_name does `_extract_country_tag` (no), then `_strip_parens` → 'america fc ' → tokens [america, fc] → uf none → state words? tokens don't include 'minas gerais' (stripped by parens removal!). Hmm — alias check happens FIRST with alias_key built from lowered text INCLUDING parens-stripped... Let me re-read my parse_team_name:\n\n```python\nlowered = normalize_text(raw)  # 'america fc (minas gerais)'\nalias_key = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9 ]\", \" \", lowered)).strip()  # 'america fc minas gerais'\nif alias_key in TEAM_ALIASES: ...\n```\nTEAM_ALIASES has 'america fc minas gerais' ✓ → ('america','MG') ✓. \n\n'Ceará Sporting Club' → alias_key 'ceara sporting club' → alias ✓ → ('ceara','CE'). ✓\n'Sport Club do Recife' → 'sport club do recife' ✓ alias.\n'São Paulo FC' → alias 'sao paulo fc' ✓.\n'Santos FC' (FIFA club is just 'Santos' though) fine.\n'Atlético Mineiro' → alias ✓. 'Atlético Paranaense' → alias ✓. 'América FC (Minas Gerais)' → alias ✓.\n'Grêmio' → bare → DEFAULT RS ✓. 'Fluminense' → DEFAULT? Not in DEFAULT_UF! base_ufs['fluminense'] = {RJ:...} single → RJ ✓ (no pin needed).\n'Bahia' → DEFAULT BA ✓. 'Vitória' → DEFAULT BA ✓. 'Botafogo' → DEFAULT RJ ✓. 'Internacional' → DEFAULT RS ✓. 'Cruzeiro' → DEFAULT MG ✓. 'Ceará Sporting Club' → alias ✓. 'Chapecoense' → DEFAULT SC ✓. 'Paraná' → DEFAULT PR ✓. 'Santos' → DEFAULT SP ✓. \n\nNow — FIFA club names observed into registry: observe('Atlético Mineiro') → alias → base 'atletico' uf 'MG' → canonical atletico-mg ✓ merged with match team Atletico-MG ✓✓. observe('Santos') → santos-sp ✓. observe('Santos Laguna') → 'santos laguna' ✓ separate. \n\nNow `brazilian_clubs_with_squads`: condition — club_id is known AND has match appearances (i.e., appears in match data). santos-sp ✓ has matches. 'paris saint germain' → is_known ✓ (observed) but no matches → excluded ✓. 'atletico madrid' → no matches ✓ excluded. 'atletico nacional' (Colombian, in Libertadores data!) → is_known + has matches (Libertadores) → INCLUDED ✗ wrong — it's not Brazilian! Need a brazilian filter: club must have a uf (Brazilian state) in canonical id. atletico-madrid → canonical 'atletico madrid'? parse 'Atlético Madrid' → tokens [atletico, madrid] no uf → base 'atletico madrid' → canonical 'atletico madrid' (no dash-uf) ✓ excluded by requiring '-' + uf in id... but 'atletico nacional' — parse: [atletico, nacional] no uf → 'atletico nacional' no uf ✓ excluded. 'nacional-uru' has suffix but not UF. So rule: canonical id ends with '-xx' where xx in BRAZILIAN_UFS (lowercase). fluminense-rj ✓. Requires DEFAULT_UF/aliases to always assign uf for Brazilian clubs — true for all Série A/B clubs via pins/single-uf. Small Brazilian clubs in cup from small states — e.g. 'Rio Branco-AC' → uf ✓. OK: `suffix = club_id.rsplit('-',1)[1].upper() in BRAZILIAN_UFS`.\n\nAlso for `squad_of('Flamengo')` — flamengo-rj has no FIFA players → empty list. The queries layer adds the helpful note listing available clubs.\n\n`player_search` club resolution — need same approach: club_ids from resolve only; if unresolved, try containment but ONLY accept clubs that resolve to the SAME base-ish... simpler: containment accepted only when resolve(club) is None. Since all FIFA clubs are observed, resolve succeeds for exact names; fuzzy partial names like 'Paris' → resolve None → containment 'paris' in 'paris saint germain' → resolve that player's club → 'paris saint germain' → add ✓ and 'paris fc' ✓. 'Santos' resolves → santos-sp only ✓. \n\nNow, also fix `_libertadores_summary` and standings. And the Copa do Brasil finals special-case. Let me rewrite store.py cleanly with these fixes. Also remove unused imports (`Iterable` from collections.abc used — yes I used it. `BR_FOOTBALL_TOURNAMENTS` imported but unused — remove. `COPA_DO_BRASIL` used in finals logic ✓).\n\nAlso `_deduplicate` merge: after swapping match/existing when priority lower, I merge fields INTO match (the keeper) from existing. Wait the loop sets `result[seen[key]] = match` after swap. And merge condition `if getattr(match, field) is None and getattr(existing, ...)` — fills keeper's missing fields from the other ✓.\n\nBut note: load order in load_all is bras, cup, lib, brf, novo — so for Série A overlaps: bras first (kept), brf later (stats merged in ✓), novo later (venue merged ✓). For cup ∩ brf: cup kept, brf stats merged ✓. \n\nWait — there's an issue with dedupe when the SAME match appears in brf with date but bras datetime... same date ✓. What about novo 2012-2019 vs bras: same dates ✓.\n\nBUT what about brf Serie A 2014-2022 vs bras 2012-2022: same matches same dates ✓ dedupe → Série A total = unique matches. 2023 only from brf. Good.\n\nOne risk: brf dates might differ from bras dates for the same fixture (data errors) → duplicates both kept → standings double-count some matches. Let me verify empirically after building: count Série A 2019 matches — should be 380. I'll check in testing.\n\nAlso for `find_matches` sorting with None dates: key (date is None, date) reverse=True — None dates go last ✓ (reverse makes True first... wait: reverse=True on (False, date) → matches with date sort first? (date is None)=False for dated → (False, d). reverse=True → larger tuples first → (True, ...) = None dates FIRST ✗. Fix: sort ascending by (date is None, date) — None last; but I want newest first among dated. Use two-stage sort: `matched.sort(key=lambda m: (m.date is None, m.date))` ascending puts dated oldest→newest, None at end; then reverse? Can't reverse whole list (None would come first). Use key=(m.date is None, m.date or date.min) reverse=True → dated newest first (date descending), then None last? (False, newest) > (False, oldest) with reverse → newest first ✓; (True, date.min) smallest → last ✓. \n\nLet me also make `standings` handle multiple competitions param: it takes a single competition name string. Default SERIE_A. match_competitions(competition)[0] — if user passes 'brasileirão' → SERIE_A ✓. If passes None → returns ALL list — standings with None competition → take [0] = Série A. OK acceptable (document default).\n\nEdge: standings for Série B/C 2014-2023 from brf — brf Serie B has 3677 matches over 2014-2023 (should be ~380/season but incomplete). Relegation = bottom 4 — for Série B that's actually relegation to Série C — the tool just reports bottom 4; queries layer labels generically. Fine.\n\nCopa do Brasil finals: precompute self._cup_final_rounds per season: max round among copa matches of that season. In stage filter: if needle in {'final','finals','finais','decisao'} and match.competition == COPA_DO_BRASIL and match.round == self._cup_final_rounds.get(match.season) → match. Also treat 'semi'/'semifinal' for cup? skip — keep 'final' only, documented.\n\nHmm wait, actually also Libertadores stage 'final' — needle 'final' matches stage text 'final' ✓ naturally.\n\nBut careful: needle 'final' with haystack for stage round-of-16 etc: `stage_needle in stage_text` — 'final' in 'quarterfinals'?? 'quarterfinals' contains 'final' ✓ → false positive! And 'semifinals' contains 'final' too. For Libertadores 'final' queries I'd get quarterfinals+semifinals+final. Fix: for stage matching use word-boundary regex or exact stage equality when needle is exactly 'final'. Approach: if stage_needle == 'final' → match.stage == 'final' (exact) or cup-final rule. Else substring on stage text. Similarly 'semifinal' → stage == 'semifinals'. Use: exact match on stage OR (needle in stage AND stage == needle + 's')... simply: `stage == needle or stage.startswith(needle)` handles final→'final'/'finals', semifinal→'semifinals' ✓ without matching quarterfinals. Round matching: needle digits → match.round == needle or f\"round {match.round}\" contains. \n\nNow queries.py — formatting layer. Then server.py, cli.py. Let me rewrite store.py with all fixes now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05aa88078001nWMgYqqTiKwIGF","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05aa648f700139ExzeDsGN5dLw"}}
