{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788227685585,"sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_f973c6ec01b541878b6a4b8a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"source venv/bin/activate && python - <<'EOF'\nfrom collections import defaultdict, Counter\nfrom brasil_mcp.store import SoccerStore\nstore = SoccerStore(\"data/kaggle\")\n\n# For each competition, how often does the same (season, home, away) appear more than once?\nseen = defaultdict(list)\nfor m in store.matches:\n    if m.season is None: continue\n    seen[(m.competition, m.season, m.home, m.away)].append((m.date, m.source))\n\nrepeat = Counter()\ngaps = Counter()\nfor key, rows in seen.items():\n    comp = key[0]\n    repeat[comp] += len(rows) > 1\n    if len(rows) > 1:\n        dates = sorted(r[0] for r in rows if r[0])\n        if len(dates) > 1:\n            gaps[(comp, (dates[1]-dates[0]).days)] += 1\nfor comp, count in repeat.items():\n    print(comp, 'same-venue pairing repeats:', count)\nprint()\nfor (comp, gap), n in sorted(gaps.items()):\n    if gap <= 60:\n        print(f\"{comp}: date gap {gap} days x{n}\")\nEOF","timeout":120000},"output":"Brasileirão Série A same-venue pairing repeats: 739\nCopa do Brasil same-venue pairing repeats: 359\nCopa Libertadores same-venue pairing repeats: 28\nBrasileirão Série B same-venue pairing repeats: 22\nBrasileirão Série C same-venue pairing repeats: 56\n\nBrasileirão Série A: date gap 1 days x701\nBrasileirão Série A: date gap 14 days x1\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 15 days x1\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 21 days x1\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 28 days x2\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 35 days x3\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 39 days x1\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 41 days x1\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 42 days x3\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 47 days x1\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 48 days x2\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 53 days x1\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 56 days x2\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 14 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 15 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 20 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 41 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 42 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 44 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 46 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 48 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 49 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 56 days x2\nCopa do Brasil: date gap 1 days x353\nCopa do Brasil: date gap 2 days x3\nCopa do Brasil: date gap 3 days x1\nCopa do Brasil: date gap 4 days x1\nCopa do Brasil: date gap 50 days x1\n","metadata":{"output":"Brasileirão Série A same-venue pairing repeats: 739\nCopa do Brasil same-venue pairing repeats: 359\nCopa Libertadores same-venue pairing repeats: 28\nBrasileirão Série B same-venue pairing repeats: 22\nBrasileirão Série C same-venue pairing repeats: 56\n\nBrasileirão Série A: date gap 1 days x701\nBrasileirão Série A: date gap 14 days x1\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 15 days x1\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 21 days x1\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 28 days x2\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 35 days x3\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 39 days x1\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 41 days x1\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 42 days x3\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 47 days x1\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 48 days x2\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 53 days x1\nBrasileirão Série C: date gap 56 days x2\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 14 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 15 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 20 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 41 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 42 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 44 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 46 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 48 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 49 days x1\nCopa Libertadores: date gap 56 days x2\nCopa do Brasil: date gap 1 days x353\nCopa do Brasil: date gap 2 days x3\nCopa do Brasil: date gap 3 days x1\nCopa do Brasil: date gap 4 days x1\nCopa do Brasil: date gap 50 days x1\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"source venv/bin/activate && python - <<'EOF'\nfrom collections import defaultdict, Counter\nfrom brasil_mcp.store import SoccerStore\nstore = SoccerStore(\"data/kaggle\")\n\n# For each competition, how often does the same (season, home, away) appear more than once?\nseen = defaultdict(list)\nfor m in store.matches:\n    if m.season is None: continue\n    seen[(m.competition, m.season, m.home, m.away)].append((m.date, m.source))\n\nrepeat = Counter()\ngaps = Counter()\nfor key, rows in seen.items():\n    comp = key[0]\n    repeat[comp] += len(rows) > 1\n    if len(rows) > 1:\n        dates = sorted(r[0] for r in rows if r[0])\n        if len(dates) > 1:\n            gaps[(comp, (dates[1]-dates[0]).days)] += 1\nfor comp, count in repeat.items():\n    print(comp, 'same-venue pairing repeats:', count)\nprint()\nfor (comp, gap), n in sorted(gaps.items()):\n    if gap <= 60:\n        print(f\"{comp}: date gap {gap} days x{n}\")\nEOF","time":{"start":1788227685565,"end":1788227685584}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I see the dedupe problem: same fixtures have DATE MISMATCHES across datasets (e.g. bras has 2019-09-23, brf has 2019-09-24 — off-by-one days, likely timezone/round-date issues). Strict (date, home, away) dedupe misses them.\n\nKey observations:\n- Each season SHOULD have 380 matches (2003-2005 had 552/462 — different formats, fine).\n- 2012/2013: bras 380 + historico 38 → the historico 38 that survived dedupe have different dates than bras. So dedupe caught 342 of 380.\n- brf leftovers every year — date mismatches.\n\nBetter dedupe strategy: for Série A (round-robin competitions), dedupe by (season, competition, home, away, round?) — no, rounds may differ across sources. Within a season+competition, a specific home/away pairing happens at most once (true double round-robin: each pairing happens twice — once each venue — so (season, competition, home, away) is unique!). For Copa do Brasil (two-legged knockout), same home/away pairing can happen twice in a season (e.g. 2012 Boavista vs América home then away — different venues so different keys; but SAME venue twice? In two legs, each team hosts once — so (season, home, away) unique per tie... unless a tie has both legs at same venue due to stadium sharing! Possible but rare; and draws/redraws? Replays don't exist in this era). Actually wait — could two different cup rounds have the same pairing & venue? Only if teams meet in two different rounds of the same cup (e.g., group+knockout — Copa do Brasil is pure knockout; but Libertadores has group stage + knockout where the same pairing occurs in group AND knockout (e.g. 2019 Flamengo vs Palestra?). YES Libertadores: same pairing can occur in group stage and knockout! (season, home, away) NOT unique for Libertadores.\n\nSo: dedupe key by competition type:\n- Série A/B/C (double round-robin): (competition, season, home, away) — safe, each venue pairing occurs once per season.\n- Copa do Brasil: two-legged; each pairing hosts once per tie, but can two clubs meet in two different rounds of the same season? No — knockout, once eliminated you're out. Two teams can only meet in one round per season. So (competition, season, home, away) unique ✓. Wait — but 2012-2021 formats: some early rounds were single-leg! Single-leg: only one match. Still unique ✓.\n- Libertadores: group stage + knockout → same pairing possible multiple times per season. Need (competition, season, home, away, stage-ish). Group matches: each pairing home+away in group stage → (home,away) unique within group stage. Knockout: same pairing across different knockout rounds? No — knockout is a tree; two teams can only meet in one knockout round... BUT the final+semifinal are two-legged, each pairing hosts once. However a pairing meeting in group stage AND knockout (e.g. 2019 Flamengo-Grêmio? or 2020?) — yes this happens. So key = (competition, season, home, away, stage) where stage differentiates group vs knockout rounds. Within 'round of 16' home/away legs: each team hosts once → (home,away) unique ✓. But 'final' 2019 single leg ✓. So Libertadores key: (season, home, away, stage-category) where stage-category = 'group stage' vs 'knockout'? If two teams meet in group AND in round of 16, stage differs ✓. If they meet in round of 16 AND quarterfinals — impossible (tree). OK: use (competition, season, home, away, stage) — but then same pairing in different stages stays separate ✓ correct.\n\nWait, but is there a risk of legitimately distinct matches collapsing? Copa do Brasil 2012 example from the head of the file: 'Boavista... vs América' round 1 leg 1 (0-0, 2012-03-07) and leg 2 'América vs Boavista' (2-1, 2012-03-14) — different home teams → different keys ✓.\n\nBut hmm, what about matches POSTPONED and replayed same venue same season in Copa do Brasil (match suspended → replayed)? In this dataset era, no replays. OK.\n\nAlso novo vs bras rounds differ but the pairing (home, away) within season is unique → key (season, home, away) merges them ✓ regardless of date mismatch.\n\nBut WAIT — there's a subtlety with 2003-2005 Série A: 552 matches = 46 rounds (24 teams? 2003 had 24 teams: 24×23=552 ✓). Still double round-robin → pairing-venue unique ✓.\n\nAnd 2005: 462 = 22 teams × 21 ✓.\n\nWhat about Série C in brf (1807 matches 2014-2023)? Série C format: 2014-2022 had group stage + knockout! Same pairing can meet in group AND playoff (e.g. 2020?). Hmm. Série C group stage: 2 groups... teams meet twice in group (home+away) + possibly in finals. So (season, home, away) NOT unique for Série C. Damn. Série B is pure double round-robin (2014+: 38 rounds ✓ 380/season expected — brf Serie B 3677/10 ≈ 368/season, slightly incomplete). Série C: knockout phases with two legs where each hosts once — within same phase pairing-venue unique; across phases (group vs playoff) can repeat!\n\nSo for Série C, key must include phase... but brf has no stage column! Only tournament. Hmm. Compromise: for Série C, use (date±1 tolerance?, home, away). Or better — use a smarter fuzzy dedupe: match on (competition, season, home, away) AND date within N days? For group-vs-playoff meetings of same pairing, dates differ by months → won't merge ✓. For cross-source duplicates, dates differ by 0-2 days → merge ✓.\n\nGeneral dedupe rule: two records are duplicates iff same competition + season + home + away + stage_category AND dates within 3 days of each other (or one date missing). For Libertadores include stage; for Série A/B/Copa do Brasil/Série B: stage_category = None. For Série C... same-pairing within 3 days but different phases? Playoffs are separate legs home/away — a pairing meeting in group AND final would be months apart ✓ safe.\n\nWait, actually simpler unified rule: duplicates iff (competition, season, home, away) match AND stage matches (for Libertadores: group/knockout category; others: same stage or one None) AND |date_a - date_b| <= 3 days. Hmm, Libertadores same pairing group stage home leg + away leg: different home/away → different key ✓.\n\nSpecial case: what about two-legged ties where BOTH legs at same stadium due to rainout relocation? Date difference >3 days typically (a week apart) ✓ safe.\n\nWhat about Libertadores 2015 Boca-River abandoned ('-' goals) — it's a distinct match ✓.\n\nOK let me also reconsider: is 3-day window safe for legitimately distinct matches? Two matches same pairing same venue within 3 days — could happen in abandoned-match replays (none in dataset) — safe.\n\nImplementation: group all matches by (competition, season, home, away); within each group, cluster by date proximity (≤3 days) and stage compatibility. For Libertadores, stage category: 'group stage' → 'group', everything else → 'knockout'? Actually just require equal non-None stages OR either None. Hmm, bras has round but no stage; novo has round; cup has round. For Série A all stages None ✓. Keep it simple:\n\nstage_compatible(a, b) = a is None or b is None or a == b\n\ncluster within group: sort by date; consecutive matches merge if date gap ≤ 3 days AND stage compatible... but gap-chaining could merge distinct matches? e.g. dates 1, 3, 5 → 1-3 merge, 3-5 merge → chains all. Pairing same venue 3 times in 5 days impossible in Brazil. Fine.\n\nPriority: keep bras > copa > lib > novo > brf and enrich.\n\nWait — one more consideration for Copa do Brasil dedupe: the same tie's two legs are (home=A,away=B) and (home=B,away=A) — distinct keys ✓. But what if a single-leg round match appears in both cup file and brf with different dates? key (competition, season, home, away) + ≤3 days merges ✓.\n\nAlso 2012-2013 historico leftovers (38 matches): date mismatches with bras > 3 days? If >3 days, still not merged. Let me check magnitude of mismatch. Let me look at one of those 2012 unmerged novo matches vs bras counterpart dates. Actually let me widen window to 7 days? Risk: Série A has rounds midweek — same pairing can't occur twice in a season so no risk at all for round-robin comps. The ONLY risk of wide window: Libertadores/Série C same-pairing-different-phase within window — impossible (phases are weeks apart). And Copa do Brasil same pairing twice same venue — never. So use 7-day window, quite safe. Actually let me even consider: for round-robin competitions (Série A/B), drop date from the key entirely — (competition, season, home, away) is already unique! Only Libertadores + Série C need date/stage disambiguation. Copa do Brasil: unique per (season, home, away) too ✓ (one tie per pairing per season, each venue once).\n\nSo the clean rule:\n- For competitions {Série A, Série B, Copa do Brasil}: key = (competition, season, home, away). Merge unconditionally.\n- For Libertadores & Série C: key = (competition, season, home, away, stage_group) + date proximity ≤ 7 days.\n  - Libertadores stage_group: 'group' if stage == 'group stage' else 'knockout' if stage else None.\n  - Série C: stage always None → group by date proximity only.\n\nHmm wait, actually for Libertadores: could the same pairing appear twice in group stage at the same venue? Group stage: 2 meetings, one per venue → (home, away) distinct ✓. Knockout two-legged: one per venue ✓. Final single leg ✓. So (season, home, away, stage_group) unique per season! No date needed for Libertadores either! Except the NA-date match (Flamengo vs Athletico final 2022? season NA). Hmm that row has season 'NA' → season None. It's the 2022 final second leg? The 2022 Libertadores final was Flamengo 1-0 Athletico (single match, Oct 29 2022, Guayaquil). The NA row: home Flamengo, away Athletico, stage final, goals '-'. And there's probably a real 2022 final row with a date. Let me check — if both exist, the NA row merges with the dated one (same season? NA season → None ≠ 2022 → different keys → both kept, one without date/result). Better: when season is None but date exists, derive season from date! For the NA row date is also NA... then it can't merge. It'll show as a separate 'unknown' final entry. Meh — acceptable: it's an unplayed/scheduled row (goals '-').\n\nActually wait — season for libertadores rows: I load season from the 'season' column. If 'NA', season=None. I could infer season from date when season missing. The NA row has no date either. Keep it as an oddity; queries with only_played filter it out; search_matches shows it (fine — it's literally in the data).\n\nFor Série C: is (season, home, away) really not unique? Let me check empirically — count Série C pairings appearing >2 times per season... Actually let me check across the brf data: same (tournament, season/date-year, home, away) appearing twice. Quick empirical check before finalizing. Also check Série B.\n\nActually simpler: let me empirically verify for ALL competitions whether (competition, season, home, away) appears more than twice (it should appear ≤ 2: once as home-A, once as home-B; same venue twice = suspicious). Count same-venue duplicates per competition, and check their date gaps to decide the rule.\n\nLet me run that analysis now, then finalize dedupe.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05aad0634001gK56LqUr8yNddD","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05aabe1f9001gb79ONYZANGTTP"}}
