{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788227719326,"sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_a8622cea410d4736babec64f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/store.py","newString":"    @staticmethod\n    def _deduplicate(matches: list[Match]) -> tuple[list[Match], int]:\n        \"\"\"Merge matches shared across datasets, keeping the richest record.\n\n        The same fixture appears in up to three files with slightly different\n        dates (timezone/data-entry drift of a day or two). Matches are grouped\n        by (competition, season, home, away) and merged when their dates are\n        at most 4 days apart, which the datasets show separates true\n        duplicates (gap <= 4 days) from legitimately distinct meetings such\n        as Libertadores group-stage vs knockout pairings (gap >= 14 days).\n        The record from the highest-priority source is kept and enriched with\n        any fields (venue, stats, kick-off time) only present in duplicates.\n        \"\"\"\n        groups: dict[tuple, list[Match]] = defaultdict(list)\n        order: list[tuple] = []\n        dated: list[Match] = []\n        for match in matches:\n            if match.date is None or match.season is None:\n                dated.append(match)\n                continue\n            key = (match.competition, match.season, match.home, match.away)\n            if key not in groups:\n                order.append(key)\n            groups[key].append(match)\n\n        result: list[Match] = []\n        duplicates = 0\n        for key in order:\n            cluster: list[Match] = []\n            last_date: date | None = None\n            for match in sorted(groups[key], key=lambda m: (m.date is None, m.date)):\n                if last_date is not None and match.date is not None and (match.date - last_date).days > 4:\n                    duplicates += _merge_cluster(cluster, result)\n                    cluster = []\n                cluster.append(match)\n                last_date = match.date or last_date\n            duplicates += _merge_cluster(cluster, result)\n        result.extend(dated)\n        return result, duplicates","oldString":"    @staticmethod\n    def _deduplicate(matches: list[Match]) -> tuple[list[Match], int]:\n        \"\"\"Merge matches shared across datasets, keeping the richest record.\n\n        Duplicates are identified by (date, home, away, competition); the\n        record from the highest-priority source is kept and enriched with any\n        fields (venue, stats, kick-off time) only present in the duplicate.\n        \"\"\"\n        seen: dict[tuple, int] = {}\n        result: list[Match] = []\n        duplicates = 0\n        for match in matches:\n            if match.date is None:\n                result.append(match)\n                continue\n            key = (match.date, match.home, match.away, match.competition)\n            if key not in seen:\n                seen[key] = len(result)\n                result.append(match)\n                continue\n            duplicates += 1\n            keeper_index = seen[key]\n            keeper = result[keeper_index]\n            other = match\n            if SOURCE_PRIORITY[other.source] < SOURCE_PRIORITY[keeper.source]:\n                keeper, other = other, keeper\n                result[keeper_index] = keeper\n            for field_name in (\n                \"venue\", \"time\", \"home_state\", \"away_state\", \"round\", \"stage\",\n                \"home_corners\", \"away_corners\", \"total_corners\", \"home_shots\",\n                \"away_shots\", \"home_attacks\", \"away_attacks\", \"ht_result\",\n                \"at_result\", \"season\",\n            ):\n                if getattr(keeper, field_name) is None and getattr(other, field_name) is not None:\n                    setattr(keeper, field_name, getattr(other, field_name))\n        return result, duplicates"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/store.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/store.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/store.py\n@@ -119,39 +119,42 @@\n @staticmethod\n def _deduplicate(matches: list[Match]) -> tuple[list[Match], int]:\n     \"\"\"Merge matches shared across datasets, keeping the richest record.\n \n-    Duplicates are identified by (date, home, away, competition); the\n-    record from the highest-priority source is kept and enriched with any\n-    fields (venue, stats, kick-off time) only present in the duplicate.\n+    The same fixture appears in up to three files with slightly different\n+    dates (timezone/data-entry drift of a day or two). Matches are grouped\n+    by (competition, season, home, away) and merged when their dates are\n+    at most 4 days apart, which the datasets show separates true\n+    duplicates (gap <= 4 days) from legitimately distinct meetings such\n+    as Libertadores group-stage vs knockout pairings (gap >= 14 days).\n+    The record from the highest-priority source is kept and enriched with\n+    any fields (venue, stats, kick-off time) only present in duplicates.\n     \"\"\"\n-    seen: dict[tuple, int] = {}\n-    result: list[Match] = []\n-    duplicates = 0\n+    groups: dict[tuple, list[Match]] = defaultdict(list)\n+    order: list[tuple] = []\n+    dated: list[Match] = []\n     for match in matches:\n-        if match.date is None:\n-            result.append(match)\n+        if match.date is None or match.season is None:\n+            dated.append(match)\n             continue\n-        key = (match.date, match.home, match.away, match.competition)\n-        if key not in seen:\n-            seen[key] = len(result)\n-            result.append(match)\n-            continue\n-        duplicates += 1\n-        keeper_index = seen[key]\n-        keeper = result[keeper_index]\n-        other = match\n-        if SOURCE_PRIORITY[other.source] < SOURCE_PRIORITY[keeper.source]:\n-            keeper, other = other, keeper\n-            result[keeper_index] = keeper\n-        for field_name in (\n-            \"venue\", \"time\", \"home_state\", \"away_state\", \"round\", \"stage\",\n-            \"home_corners\", \"away_corners\", \"total_corners\", \"home_shots\",\n-            \"away_shots\", \"home_attacks\", \"away_attacks\", \"ht_result\",\n-            \"at_result\", \"season\",\n-        ):\n-            if getattr(keeper, field_name) is None and getattr(other, field_name) is not None:\n-                setattr(keeper, field_name, getattr(other, field_name))\n+        key = (match.competition, match.season, match.home, match.away)\n+        if key not in groups:\n+            order.append(key)\n+        groups[key].append(match)\n+\n+    result: list[Match] = []\n+    duplicates = 0\n+    for key in order:\n+        cluster: list[Match] = []\n+        last_date: date | None = None\n+        for match in sorted(groups[key], key=lambda m: (m.date is None, m.date)):\n+            if last_date is not None and match.date is not None and (match.date - last_date).days > 4:\n+                duplicates += _merge_cluster(cluster, result)\n+                cluster = []\n+            cluster.append(match)\n+            last_date = match.date or last_date\n+        duplicates += _merge_cluster(cluster, result)\n+    result.extend(dated)\n     return result, duplicates\n \n def resolve_team(self, name: str | None) -> str | None:\n     return self.registry.resolve(name) if name else None\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/store.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/store.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/store.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/store.py\n@@ -119,39 +119,42 @@\n @staticmethod\n def _deduplicate(matches: list[Match]) -> tuple[list[Match], int]:\n     \"\"\"Merge matches shared across datasets, keeping the richest record.\n \n-    Duplicates are identified by (date, home, away, competition); the\n-    record from the highest-priority source is kept and enriched with any\n-    fields (venue, stats, kick-off time) only present in the duplicate.\n+    The same fixture appears in up to three files with slightly different\n+    dates (timezone/data-entry drift of a day or two). Matches are grouped\n+    by (competition, season, home, away) and merged when their dates are\n+    at most 4 days apart, which the datasets show separates true\n+    duplicates (gap <= 4 days) from legitimately distinct meetings such\n+    as Libertadores group-stage vs knockout pairings (gap >= 14 days).\n+    The record from the highest-priority source is kept and enriched with\n+    any fields (venue, stats, kick-off time) only present in duplicates.\n     \"\"\"\n-    seen: dict[tuple, int] = {}\n-    result: list[Match] = []\n-    duplicates = 0\n+    groups: dict[tuple, list[Match]] = defaultdict(list)\n+    order: list[tuple] = []\n+    dated: list[Match] = []\n     for match in matches:\n-        if match.date is None:\n-            result.append(match)\n+        if match.date is None or match.season is None:\n+            dated.append(match)\n             continue\n-        key = (match.date, match.home, match.away, match.competition)\n-        if key not in seen:\n-            seen[key] = len(result)\n-            result.append(match)\n-            continue\n-        duplicates += 1\n-        keeper_index = seen[key]\n-        keeper = result[keeper_index]\n-        other = match\n-        if SOURCE_PRIORITY[other.source] < SOURCE_PRIORITY[keeper.source]:\n-            keeper, other = other, keeper\n-            result[keeper_index] = keeper\n-        for field_name in (\n-            \"venue\", \"time\", \"home_state\", \"away_state\", \"round\", \"stage\",\n-            \"home_corners\", \"away_corners\", \"total_corners\", \"home_shots\",\n-            \"away_shots\", \"home_attacks\", \"away_attacks\", \"ht_result\",\n-            \"at_result\", \"season\",\n-        ):\n-            if getattr(keeper, field_name) is None and getattr(other, field_name) is not None:\n-                setattr(keeper, field_name, getattr(other, field_name))\n+        key = (match.competition, match.season, match.home, match.away)\n+        if key not in groups:\n+            order.append(key)\n+        groups[key].append(match)\n+\n+    result: list[Match] = []\n+    duplicates = 0\n+    for key in order:\n+        cluster: list[Match] = []\n+        last_date: date | None = None\n+        for match in sorted(groups[key], key=lambda m: (m.date is None, m.date)):\n+            if last_date is not None and match.date is not None and (match.date - last_date).days > 4:\n+                duplicates += _merge_cluster(cluster, result)\n+                cluster = []\n+            cluster.append(match)\n+            last_date = match.date or last_date\n+        duplicates += _merge_cluster(cluster, result)\n+    result.extend(dated)\n     return result, duplicates\n \n def resolve_team(self, name: str | None) -> str | None:\n     return self.registry.resolve(name) if name else None\n","additions":31,"deletions":28},"truncated":false},"title":"src/brasil_mcp/store.py","time":{"start":1788227719323,"end":1788227719325}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The pattern is crystal clear:\n- Date gap of 1-4 days = cross-source duplicates (timezone/data-entry drift): 701 in Série A, 353 in Copa do Brasil.\n- Date gaps ≥ 14 days = legitimate distinct meetings (Série C group+playoff phases, Libertadores group+knockout, and a couple of odd cases like the 14-day Série A gap and 50-day Copa gap).\n\nInteresting: Série A has ONE 14-day gap — a legit case? Same pairing same venue twice in a season 14 days apart — probably a data error in one of the sources, or a rescheduled match where both the original and new date exist. Keep it separate (conservative).\n\nSo the dedupe rule:\n- Group by (competition, season, home, away).\n- Merge records within a group if their dates differ by ≤ 4 days (or either is None), merging greedily by sorted date.\n- Also merge if scores are identical and dates within, say, 10 days? No — keep it simple, ≤4 days.\n\nWhat about the NA-date Libertadores final row (season None)? Group key uses season — None groups separately. Fine.\n\nFor None-date matches with same key as dated ones: merge them (the NA row would merge into the dated 2022 final if season matched — it doesn't since its season is None). Leave as-is.\n\nImplementation plan for _deduplicate:\n```python\ngroups = defaultdict(list)\nfor match in matches: groups[(competition, season, home, away)].append(match)\nfor each group: sort by (date is None, date); cluster: start cluster with first; for each next, if (date is None or cluster's last date is None or (next.date - cluster_last.date).days <= 4) → merge into cluster; else start new cluster.\n```\nWait — but if cluster has multiple dates, compare against the latest date in cluster. Simpler: compare with the previous element's date (chain). Dates sorted ascending; gap ≤4 merges. Chaining risk (1,3,5,7...): impossible in practice since same pairing can't play that often.\n\nBut careful about None dates: match with None date merges into the cluster unconditionally? A None-date match (like the NA final) with season 2022 would merge into the 2022 final cluster — actually GOOD (it's the same final). But it could also wrongly merge if a None-date row is spurious. Only one None-date row exists in the data (libertadores NA final), and its season is None too → own group. Either way safe.\n\nFor ordering priority when merging: keep highest-priority source record as the base; enrich with others' fields. Also when merging, prefer the record with a date over None.\n\nAlso — merging None dates: if the keeper has None date but other has date, fill date! Add \"date\" to the merge field list... but my merge loop sets fields only if keeper's is None. Add \"date\" and \"time\" to the fillable fields. Since I pick keeper by priority, a None-date keeper (from bras) with a dated duplicate (from brf) gets the date filled ✓.\n\nOrdering of result: keep original insertion order? The result list order affects nothing much (queries sort). I'll append clusters in first-seen order.\n\nOne more thing — after dedupe, season totals should be ~380 for 2012-2022. Let me also handle: what if the keeper is from 'brasileirao' with date D1, dup from 'brasileirao_historico' with date D2 (≠D1, ≤4 days)? Keeper keeps its own date ✓ (only fill if None).\n\nWhich source has the \"correct\" date? Doesn't matter much for queries.\n\nAlso the score: keeper keeps its own goals; if keeper unplayed (None) and dup played, fill goals too! Add home_goals/away_goals to fillable fields. The NA final: if grouped (it isn't), goals would fill. Add anyway for robustness.\n\nLet me rewrite _deduplicate.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05aad908d0012Y1YhbZtl3Nbg2","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05aad0e2a001ygvB6FsWhYyjsZ"}}
