{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788227858649,"sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_62390721b73c4511ba3530d0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"source venv/bin/activate && python - <<'EOF'\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom brasil_mcp.store import SoccerStore\nstore = SoccerStore(\"data/kaggle\")\n\nseen = defaultdict(list)\nfor m in store.matches:\n    seen[(m.competition, m.season, m.home, m.away)].append(m)\n\nfor key, rows in sorted(seen.items()):\n    if len(rows) > 1 and key[0] == \"Brasileirão Série A\" and key[1] in (2012, 2013, 2015, 2018, 2019):\n        for m in rows:\n            print(key[1], m.source, m.date, m.home_display, m.away_display, m.home_goals, m.away_goals, 'round', m.round, 'venue', m.venue)\n        print('---')\nEOF","timeout":120000},"output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 9, in <module>\nTypeError: '<' not supported between instances of 'NoneType' and 'int'\n","metadata":{"output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 9, in <module>\nTypeError: '<' not supported between instances of 'NoneType' and 'int'\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"source venv/bin/activate && python - <<'EOF'\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom brasil_mcp.store import SoccerStore\nstore = SoccerStore(\"data/kaggle\")\n\nseen = defaultdict(list)\nfor m in store.matches:\n    seen[(m.competition, m.season, m.home, m.away)].append(m)\n\nfor key, rows in sorted(seen.items()):\n    if len(rows) > 1 and key[0] == \"Brasileirão Série A\" and key[1] in (2012, 2013, 2015, 2018, 2019):\n        for m in rows:\n            print(key[1], m.source, m.date, m.home_display, m.away_display, m.home_goals, m.away_goals, 'round', m.round, 'venue', m.venue)\n        print('---')\nEOF","time":{"start":1788227858630,"end":1788227858647}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now everything is clear:\n\n1. **Série A 2020** runs 2020-08-08 → 2021-02-25 (bras is authoritative). brf's Jan-Feb 2021 \"Serie A\" records are 2020-season matches. Fix: for Série A/B/C from brf, if month is Jan or Feb → season = year - 1.\n\n2. **Copa do Brasil finals are genuinely early-year**: the 2020 final was Feb 28 + Mar 7, 2021 — the CUP FILE (authoritative) labels it season 2020, round 8. brf labels those matches 2021 (calendar year). Also brf has Jan/Feb Copa matches in 2015, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2022, 2023 — those are probably early rounds of the season labeled by calendar year... e.g. Copa do Brasil 2015 first round was Feb/Mar 2015 → labeled 2015 by both? The cup file 2015 season starts Feb? Let me think: Copa do Brasil first rounds happen in Feb-Mar of the season year, so calendar year == season year for most. Only the 2020 final (Mar 2021) is mislabeled by brf. The Grêmio-Palmeiras Mar 2021 matches in brf (labeled 2021) = 2020 final (cup file: 2020-02-28 & 2020-03-07 season 2020).\n\n   Wait, dates differ slightly: cup file has 2021-02-28 and 2021-03-07; brf has 2021-03-01 and 2021-03-07. Gap of 1 day on the first leg (Feb 28 vs Mar 1). With season fixed to 2020 for both, my dedupe (key + ≤4 days) would merge them ✓.\n\n   So for brf Copa do Brasil: which Jan/Feb/Mar records should map to season-1? ONLY the 2020 final (Mar 2021). Copa 2015 first round: Feb 2015 belongs to season 2015 (cup file 2015 season — starts when? let me check cup season windows). If cup 2015 season starts 2015-02-08, then a brf Feb 2015 match labeled 2015 is correct ✓. So the rule \"month ≤ 2 → season-1\" would WRONGLY shift brf Copa Feb 2015 matches to 2014!\n\n   Solution: use the authoritative source (cup file) season windows. For brf Copa records, assign season = season of the cup file whose window [min_date, max_date] (padded) contains the date; fall back to brf's own label. Actually — more robust general approach: for ALL brf records, cross-check against authoritative windows per competition:\n\n   For each brf match (competition, date):\n   - Look up authoritative windows for that competition (from bras+novo for Série A; cup file for Copa do Brasil; lib file for Libertadores; none for Série B/C — brf only).\n   - If a window [start - 30d, end + 30d] contains the date → use that window's season.\n   - Else keep brf's own label.\n\n   For Copa 2020: window = [2020-02-25?..2021-03-07] wait cup 2020 season window from cup file: 2020 season started ~Jan/Feb 2020? and ended 2021-03-07. So the 2020 window includes Mar 2021 ✓ → brf Mar 2021 → season 2020 ✓. And the 2021 cup window starts ~Feb/Mar 2021? If cup 2021 window starts BEFORE 2021-03-07, there'd be ambiguity (two windows contain the date). Order matters: prefer the window where the date fits within [start-30, end+30]; if multiple, prefer... For the 2020 final legs (Feb 28/Mar 1 + Mar 7 2021): cup 2021 window — when did the 2021 cup start? Probably 2021-03-03 (first round). So Mar 2021 falls in both [2020 window padded] and [2021 window]. Ugh.\n\n   Hmm. But wait — for dedupe purposes, what matters most is that the brf 2020-final legs MERGE with the cup-file 2020-final legs. If brf keeps season=2021 for them, they won't merge (different key). But if I instead RELY on my dedupe with a different strategy for copa: same (home, away) pairing within ±4 days but different season labels... \n\n   Alternative cleaner approach: do the dedupe FIRST on (competition, home, away, date±4d) IGNORING season, then take the season from the highest-priority source. The season only participates via the authoritative source. For legitimate distinct meetings (Libertadores group vs knockout; Série C group vs playoff), dates are ≥14 days apart, so a date-proximity dedupe WITHOUT season in the key still works... but Série C 2020-vs-2021 boundary: a Série C match Feb 2021 (season 2020 tail) vs Mar 2021 (season 2021 start) — if same pairing same venue 3 weeks apart?? Série C: group stage 2021 started May 2021. Fine.\n\n   But there's a subtle risk without season in key: same pairing+venue in consecutive seasons with dates within 4 days (season boundary mid-month). E.g. Copa do Brasil 2020 final Mar 7 2021 vs Copa 2021 first round Mar 9 2021 same pairing? Vanishingly unlikely.\n\n   Simplest robust fix combining both insights:\n   1. brf season correction: for Série A, Série B, Série C: if month <= 2 → season - 1. (Série A/B/C seasons never have Jan/Feb matches belonging to their own calendar year — verified: bras min dates are Apr/May, and 2020 season ended Feb 25 2021. Série B similar. Série C 2020 ended... let me assume same pattern; Jan/Feb Série C matches in brf are only 2021 (=2020 tail).) \n      Wait — what about Série D? not in data. OK.\n      Hmm, but brf 'Serie A' Jan/Feb 2016?? The output shows ('Serie A', '2016') — a Jan or Feb 2016 Série A match?! 2015 season ended Dec 6 2015; 2016 season started May 14. A Jan/Feb 2016 \"Serie A\" match in brf — data error or... let me look at it specifically. It might be a mislabeled match (e.g., a friendly or CdB match tagged wrong in brf). With my rule it'd become season 2015 — could duplicate a 2015 season match or add a phantom. Let me inspect that record.\n   2. Copa do Brasil from brf: use the cup-file season windows to relabel (window containment, preferring the latest window whose start ≤ date ≤ end+45d or so). Or special-case: only relabel if a same-pairing cup-file match exists within ±4 days with a different season → then adopt that season. That's very targeted and safe!\n\n   Actually here's an even more precise general solution: **two-pass dedupe**:\n   - Pass 1: index all matches from authoritative sources (bras, novo, cup, lib) by (competition, home, away, date±4d window). For each brf match, look for an authoritative match with same (competition, home, away) within 4 days → if found, it's a duplicate: merge and DISCARD brf's season/round in favor of the authoritative one.\n   - Pass 2: for remaining matches, group by (competition, season, home, away) with ≤4-day clustering (same as current).\n\n   This handles brf season mislabels automatically! Because merge takes season from the priority source. And authoritative-vs-authoritative dupes (bras vs novo, bras vs cup) have consistent season labels mostly... but do they? novo 2012-2019 vs bras 2012-2019: same seasons ✓. cup vs brf: handled by pass 1 ✓.\n\n   But wait — the unmerged 38 novo leftovers in 2012/2013/2015/2018/2019 (gap > 4 days from bras counterpart)? Those are matches where novo and bras dates differ by MORE than 4 days?? From the gap histogram after old dedupe: Série A gap 1 x701, gap 14 x1 — so after merging same-key with any gap? no wait. Hmm, the old dedupe merged only exact same-date. The repeats that REMAINED after old dedupe: 739 with mostly gap-1. Now new dedupe (≤4 days) fixed gap ≤4. The leftover +38 per season 2012/2013/2015/2018/2019: these are same (season, home, away) pairs with gap > 4 days — from the new remaining-gaps histogram: gaps of 62-324 days etc. (the big histogram). Wait, but that histogram was computed across ALL competitions. For Série A specifically, the samples shown were all 2021 brf mislabels (Jan/Feb 2021 vs May 2021). The novo leftovers: hmm, 2012 has 418 = 380 + 38. Which source? Earlier per-season source table (after old dedupe): 2012: brasileirao 380 + historico 38. So 38 novo records unmerged in 2012. With new dedupe... let me recheck the new per-season counts — I didn't print sources this time. The 418s could be brf mislabels (2021-style) — no, 2012? brf covers 2014+. So 2012's +38 must be novo-vs-bras mismatches with gaps > 4 days?? But gap histogram for Série A showed only gap-1 and gap-14...\n\n   Oh wait — I bet the issue is season attribution in NOVO for 2012/2013: novo 2012 might include matches that bras 2012 doesn't (postponed?) or dates differ wildly. OR: the +38 in 2012 are round-38 matches played in DECEMBER vs... Hmm. Let me just directly examine the 2012 unmerged extras.\n\nLet me look at the actual data.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05aafaa18001aP64Ei6OgQcO80","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05aaed826001IiO5mB6e6N0qLZ"}}
