 -4","time":{"start":1788227907309,"end":1788227907310}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The 2012 novo-only pairs are ALL \"X vs vasco-rj\" — Vasco's AWAY matches?? No wait, home=X, away=vasco-rj — Vasco away games. All 19 teams vs Vasco + ... 38 pairs. Interesting: novo 2012 has 38 matches where away = vasco-rj?? A season has 19 distinct \"X vs Vasco\" home pairings. 38 = 19×2 — maybe Vasco appears twice per opponent? OR novo's 2012 Vasco home games ('vasco-rj' as home) ALSO unmerged? The novo-only list shows all pairs with away=vasco-rj... plus 19 more pairs probably with home=vasco-rj. And where are they in bras? If bras 2012 has (home='vasco-rj', away='botafogo-rj') and novo has the same, they'd merge. So novo-only pairs = 38 all involving vasco.\n\nTHE BUG: Vasco's name in bras is \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" → alias 'vasco da gama' → ('vasco','RJ') → 'vasco-rj'. In novo: 'Vasco' → base 'vasco' no uf → _resolve_uf('vasco'): DEFAULT_UF['vasco']... did I include 'vasco'? Looking at my DEFAULT_UF: yes, \"vasco\": \"RJ\" ✓. Hmm so both → vasco-rj.\n\nWait — the pairs are novo-only, meaning the SAME pair (e.g. 'botafogo-rj','vasco-rj') exists in novo 2012 but NOT in bras 2012. So bras 2012 must encode these pairings differently — maybe as (home='vasco-rj', away='botafogo-rj')... no, that's the REVERSE pairing (Vasco home). In a double round-robin, each pairing occurs once per venue. (botafogo-rj, vasco-rj) means Botafogo home vs Vasco away. If novo has it and bras doesn't, then bras 2012 must have a DIFFERENT canonical for one of the teams in that fixture!\n\nHmm wait, actually look: novo-only pairs ALL have away=vasco-rj. So every novo \"X vs Vasco (Vasco away)\" match has no bras counterpart. Which means in bras, the same fixture has Vasco resolving to something ELSE... but I showed both files → vasco-rj. Unless... the HOME team differs! E.g., bras home_team for those fixtures — is 'Botafogo-RJ' → botafogo-rj ✓ same.\n\nOR the issue is DATES: dedupe merges by pairing regardless of date... wait no! My dedupe key is (competition, season, home, away) — I merge unconditionally within 4 days only! The novo X-vs-Vasco matches might have dates >4 days apart from bras counterparts!! Look at the output: pairs are missing from `bras` set entirely — the pairing (botafogo-rj, vasco-rj) not in bras 2012 pairs at all? That can't be, Botafogo hosted Vasco in 2012...\n\nHold on, let me recheck: `extra_novo = novo - bras` — these pairings exist in NOVO but NOT in BRAS. Let me verify Botafogo×Vasco 2012 in the bras file directly. Actually — maybe the issue: in bras file, the team is written \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\"?? I handled that with alias. Let me check raw. Actually let me just grep the bras file for Vasco 2012 rows.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ab06eb60016Wat6g8lifI11b","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05ab01a22001iFBD96xN3RP2nD"}}
