s that share a word and differ by 'da/de/do' or truncations.\n\nActually the cleanest general fix: in `_drop_legal_words`, ALSO drop Portuguese prepositions {'de','da','do','dos','das','e'} — wait, that changes 'bahia de feira' → 'bahia feira' consistently everywhere, fine. But 'vasco da gama' → 'vasco gama' still needs mapping to 'vasco'. So still need an alias.\n\nBetter general approach: TRUNCATION aliasing — if a base B1 ends with/starts with... no, too fuzzy.\n\nLet me find ALL the mismatch cases empirically: for each date+competition, compare pairings across files and find unmerged same-date fixtures. Then build targeted aliases. Let me write that analysis: match by (date±1, competition) and home/away sets — find fixtures present in 2+ sources where canonicals differ, print the raw name pairs that caused the mismatch.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ab0f7f8001xGX9xPRzHtPHny","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05ab07042001idbFKGWp77RDp2"}}
