rts when? Let me check cup season windows. If cup 2021 starts March 2021 too, ambiguity. Resolve ambiguity by preferring the window with the LATER max_date? For 2021-03-01: windows 2020 (ends 2021-03-07, padded to Apr 6) and 2021 (starts ~2021-03-03, padded to Feb 1). Both contain. Prefer window where date is closer to the end? The 2020 final belongs to 2020. Hmm — but a brf match 2021-03-10 (2021 first round) also fits 2020-window-padded (Apr 6) and 2021 window. Can't disambiguate reliably by window.\n\nAlternative targeted approach for copa: match brf copa records to cup-file records directly: same (home, away) ± 4 days → adopt the cup-file record's season. That's exactly the dedupe! So: make dedupe season-agnostic in a pre-pass:\n  Pre-pass: for each brf match with season S and date D, search OTHER-source matches (non-brf) with same (competition, home, away) and |date diff| ≤ 4 → if found, retarget the brf match's season to the found match's season (and let normal dedupe merge them).\n  \nThis handles both copa-2020-final and Série A/B/C Jan-Feb 2021 cases (brf Jan 2021 Serie A → matches bras 2020-season match ±4d? The bras 2020 season ended 2021-02-25; brf Jan/Feb 2021 Série A records correspond to bras 2020-season records — same pairing, dates within a day or two ✓ → retarget season to 2020 ✓).\n\nWhat if no counterpart exists (brf-only matches like 2023)? Keep brf's label but apply the month≤2 → year-1 heuristic for Série A/B/C (brf 2023 Jan/Feb Serie C matches → 2022 season ✓ sensible).\n\nSérie C 2020: ended Jan 2021? brf 'Serie C' Jan/Feb 2021 → retarget to a lib/cup/bras match? Série C only exists in brf — no authoritative counterpart! The retarget pre-pass finds nothing → fallback heuristic month≤2 → 2020 ✓.\n\nBut Série C matches in Feb 2021 belonging to season... Série C 2020 actually finished in Jan 2021 (I believe the 2020 Série C finals were Jan 2021). OK.\n\nAlso what about brf Série B Jan/Feb 2021 (2020 tail)? Retarget pre-pass: Série B only in brf → no counterpart → fallback month≤2 → 2020 ✓.\n\nImplementation: rather than a separate pre-pass, do it inside SoccerStore before dedupe:\n```python\ndef _reconcile_brf_seasons(matches):\n    # index non-brf matches by (competition, home, away) -> list of (date, season)\n    index = defaultdict(list)\n    for m in matches:\n        if m.source != 'br_football' and m.date and m.season:\n            index[(m.competition, m.home, m.away)].append((m.date, m.season))\n    for m in matches:\n        if m.source == 'br_football' and m.date and m.season:\n            key = (m.competition, m.home, m.away)\n            for date, season in index.get(key, ()):  # find within 4 days\n                if abs((m.date - date).days) <= 4 and season != m.season:\n                    m.season = season\n                    break\n            else:\n                if m.date.month <= 2 and m.competition != COPA_DO_BRASIL:\n                    m.season = m.date.year - 1\n                elif m.date.month <= 2 and m.competition == COPA_DO_BRASIL:\n                    # early-year copa matches usually belong to that calendar year's cup\n                    m.season = m.season  # keep\n```\nWait — copa Jan/Feb matches (2015, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2022, 2023 years listed): those are first rounds of that year's cup → keep label ✓ (retarget handles 2020-final case). \n\nHmm wait, one flaw: retarget loop `for date, season in index.get(key)` — need closest match, not first within 4 days; but within 4 days any is fine (seasons of counterparts within 4 days of the same fixture are consistent).\n\nAlso apply retarget BEFORE dedupe. And the heuristic: for Série A/B/C month≤2 → year-1. What about month==12? Season Y ends Dec — label Y ✓ correct. Month 3: Série A starts late March/April — a March 3 match labeled Y: could it be season Y-1's tail? Only 2020 season ended Feb 25 2021 — no March. Cup 2020 ended Mar 7 2021 — copa handled by retarget (cup file counterpart). But what if a brf copa match from the 2020 final has no ±4d counterpart? Both legs exist in cup file, so retarget works.\n\nEdge: brf copa 2021-03-07 leg2 — cup file 2020-03-07 ✓ retargets. brf copa 2021-03-01 leg1 — cup 2021-02-28 diff 1 day ✓ retargets.\n\nNow — also Série A brf 2016 Jan/Feb ('Serie A','2016' in the early list!): a Jan/Feb 2016 Série A match in brf — there was NO Série A in Jan 2016 (2015 ended Dec 6, 2016 started May). This is likely a brf data error (mislabeled tournament). With my heuristic it becomes season 2015 — could that create a phantom duplicate of a real 2015 match? If it's a real 2015-season match with wrong date in brf, dedupe might not merge (different date) → standings 2015 gets an extra match (381). Meh — data quality issue in source; acceptable. Let me check what that match is. Actually the new per-season count for 2015 was 418 — +38 over 380. 38 = 2×19. Hmm interesting — 2015: 418. Maybe brf 2015 Jan/Feb 'Serie A' matches are actually the 2014 tail?? No — 2014 season ended Dec 7 2014. Jan/Feb 2015 Série A matches can't be 2014-season. Wait, brf tournament label 'Serie A' might actually include 'Serie A' matches from other competitions mislabeled. Let me look at those specific records before finalizing.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ab2d204001w3VvTdEeNP43E0","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05ab1017c001r515H5XIrv7vh9"}}
