{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788228158174,"sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_376e5aa0001649ffb838ea5d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/normalize.py","newString":"    def _base_is_ambiguous(self, cid: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"True when a base name is shared by clubs of different states.\n\n        A club holding >= 80% of a base's observations is considered the\n        dominant club and keeps the clean unsuffixed display (e.g. 'Santos');\n        minor sharers show the state suffix (e.g. 'Santos-AP').\n        \"\"\"\n        base = cid.rsplit(\"-\", 1)[0] if \"-\" in cid else cid\n        ufs = self._base_ufs.get(base)\n        if not ufs:\n            return False\n        counts = {u: c for u, c in ufs.items() if u}\n        if len(counts) <= 1:\n            return False\n        total = sum(counts.values())\n        if not total:\n            return False\n        top = max(counts.values())\n        return top / total < 0.8","oldString":"    def _base_is_ambiguous(self, cid: str) -> bool:\n        base = cid.rsplit(\"-\", 1)[0] if \"-\" in cid else cid\n        ufs = self._base_ufs.get(base)\n        if not ufs:\n            return False\n        return len({u for u in ufs if u}) > 1"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -347,13 +347,26 @@\n         display = re.sub(r\"\\s+-\\s+([A-Za-z]{2,3})$\", r\"-\\1\", display)\n         self._displays[cid] = display\n \n def _base_is_ambiguous(self, cid: str) -> bool:\n+    \"\"\"True when a base name is shared by clubs of different states.\n+\n+    A club holding >= 80% of a base's observations is considered the\n+    dominant club and keeps the clean unsuffixed display (e.g. 'Santos');\n+    minor sharers show the state suffix (e.g. 'Santos-AP').\n+    \"\"\"\n     base = cid.rsplit(\"-\", 1)[0] if \"-\" in cid else cid\n     ufs = self._base_ufs.get(base)\n     if not ufs:\n         return False\n-    return len({u for u in ufs if u}) > 1\n+    counts = {u: c for u, c in ufs.items() if u}\n+    if len(counts) <= 1:\n+        return False\n+    total = sum(counts.values())\n+    if not total:\n+        return False\n+    top = max(counts.values())\n+    return top / total < 0.8\n \n def display(self, cid: str) -> str:\n     \"\"\"Human-friendly display name for a canonical id.\"\"\"\n     return self._displays.get(cid, cid.replace(\"-\", \" \").title())\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/normalize.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -347,13 +347,26 @@\n         display = re.sub(r\"\\s+-\\s+([A-Za-z]{2,3})$\", r\"-\\1\", display)\n         self._displays[cid] = display\n \n def _base_is_ambiguous(self, cid: str) -> bool:\n+    \"\"\"True when a base name is shared by clubs of different states.\n+\n+    A club holding >= 80% of a base's observations is considered the\n+    dominant club and keeps the clean unsuffixed display (e.g. 'Santos');\n+    minor sharers show the state suffix (e.g. 'Santos-AP').\n+    \"\"\"\n     base = cid.rsplit(\"-\", 1)[0] if \"-\" in cid else cid\n     ufs = self._base_ufs.get(base)\n     if not ufs:\n         return False\n-    return len({u for u in ufs if u}) > 1\n+    counts = {u: c for u, c in ufs.items() if u}\n+    if len(counts) <= 1:\n+        return False\n+    total = sum(counts.values())\n+    if not total:\n+        return False\n+    top = max(counts.values())\n+    return top / total < 0.8\n \n def display(self, cid: str) -> str:\n     \"\"\"Human-friendly display name for a canonical id.\"\"\"\n     return self._displays.get(cid, cid.replace(\"-\", \" \").title())\n","additions":14,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"src/brasil_mcp/normalize.py","time":{"start":1788228158171,"end":1788228158173}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait, there's an issue with `_base_is_ambiguous` for the display: for 'santos-sp', base 'santos' has ufs {SP, AP} → ambiguous → display uses suffixed form 'Santos-SP' ✓ good. For 'palmeiras-sp', base 'palmeiras' ufs {SP} → unambiguous → unsuffixed 'Palmeiras' ✓. For 'atletico-mg': base 'atletico' has {GO, MG, PR} → ambiguous → display 'Atletico-MG' or 'Atlético - MG'→tidied 'Atlético-MG' ✓. Hmm — I'd like the accented 'Atlético-MG'. Frequency decides. Fine.\n\nAlso 'flamengo-rj' vs 'flamengo-pi': base 'flamengo' ufs {RJ, PI} → ambiguous → 'Flamengo-RJ' ✓ (correct, distinguishes from Flamengo-PI).\n\nHmm, but the Série A big teams will display with suffixes: 'Flamengo-RJ', 'Corinthians-SP', 'São Paulo-SP'... because their bases are \"ambiguous\" (Flamengo-PI, Santos-AP, Botafogo-PB, América multiple, Vasco? just RJ... wait 'vasco' base: only RJ → 'Vasco' ✓; 'fluminense' only RJ → 'Fluminense' ✓; 'corinthians' only SP → 'Corinthians' ✓; 'sao paulo' only SP → 'São Paulo' ✓; 'palmeiras' only SP ✓; 'cruzeiro' only MG ✓; 'gremio' only RS ✓; 'internacional' only RS ✓; 'bahia' base has {BA} only? 'Bahia de Feira' is base 'bahia de feira' — different base ✓ → 'Bahia' ✓; 'flamengo' {RJ, PI} → 'Flamengo-RJ'; 'santos' {SP, AP} → 'Santos-SP'; 'botafogo' {RJ, PB} → 'Botafogo-RJ'; 'america' {MG, RN} → 'América-MG'; 'atletico' {MG, PR, GO} → suffixed; 'vitoria' {BA, ES} → 'Vitória-BA'; 'sport' {PE} → 'Sport' ✓; 'nautico' {PE, RR} → 'Náutico-PE'; 'juventude' {RS, MA} → 'Juventude-RS'... \n\nHmm, showing 'Santos-SP' instead of 'Santos' in standings is slightly less pretty but unambiguous and defensible. The spec example shows \"Santos\" and \"Flamengo\" in standings. Since the famous club is nearly always intended, maybe better: display without suffix for the DOMINANT club (highest match count) even if ambiguous, and with suffix for the minor one. E.g., 'santos-sp' (huge) → 'Santos'; 'santos-ap' (tiny) → 'Santos-AP'. That gives prettier output for famous clubs while keeping disambiguation where it matters. Dominance by total canonical count: compare counts of 'santos-sp' vs 'santos-ap' raw observations. If one has >80% share → no suffix in display.\n\nLet me implement: `_base_is_ambiguous` → returns True only if the minority share ≥ 20%. I'll compute share from _canonical_raws counts... but _base_ufs counts are per base across all ufs. For base 'santos': Counter({'SP': 5000, 'AP': 20}) → SP share 99.6% → not ambiguous → 'Santos'. For 'america': MG vs RN — RN has decent presence (Série B/C) → maybe 30%? → ambiguous → 'América-MG'. For 'botafogo': RJ dominant, PB minor → 'Botafogo'. For 'atletico': three-way → suffixed ✓. For 'nautico': PE vs RR — RR has some Série C presence → depends. For 'flamengo': RJ huge vs PI tiny → 'Flamengo' ✓. \n\nImplement: share = max_uf_count / total_nonempty_count; ambiguous iff share < 0.8.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ab442d5001UCoghkjLxJIxI5","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05ab3e5b6001L5nfbI2y01r9Rl"}}
