==========\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -111,10 +111,10 @@\n \"santa cruz futebol clube\": (\"santa cruz\", \"PE\"),\n \"red bull brasil\": (\"bragantino\", \"SP\"),\n \"red bull bragantino\": (\"bragantino\", \"SP\"),\n \"rb bragantino\": (\"bragantino\", \"SP\"),\n-\"atletico goianiense\": (\"atletico goianiense\", \"GO\"),\n-\"atletico clube goianiense\": (\"atletico goianiense\", \"GO\"),\n+\"atletico goianiense\": (\"atletico\", \"GO\"),\n+\"atletico clube goianiense\": (\"atletico\", \"GO\"),\n \"guarani fc\": (\"guarani\", \"SP\"),\n \"figueirense fc\": (\"figueirense\", \"SC\"),\n \"associacao portuguesa de desportos\": (\"portuguesa\", \"SP\"),\n \"flamengo do piaui\": (\"flamengo\", \"PI\"),\n","additions":2,"deletions":2},"truncated":false},"title":"src/brasil_mcp/normalize.py","time":{"start":1788228282880,"end":1788228282894}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Found it — a name-resolution split, not mislabeled data!\n\n'Atletico Goianiense' (brf) resolves to canonical 'atletico goianiense-go' while bras uses 'Atletico-GO' → 'atletico-go'. TWO different canonicals for the same club! From my earlier scan: \n```\n## atletico (go):\n   'atletico goianiense-go'                 <- 'Atletico Goianiense'\n   'atletico-go'                            <- 'Atletico-GO' / 'Atlético - GO' / 'Atlético-GO'\n```\n\nMy alias table has \"atletico goianiense\": (\"atletico goianiense\", \"GO\") — that's the bug I introduced! It should map to (\"atletico\", \"GO\"). Same for \"atletico clube goianiense\".\n\nFix: \"atletico goianiense\" → (\"atletico\", \"GO\").\n\nThen 2017 Série A: 380 ✓. Similarly 2020/2021/2022 extras might be other alias bugs — let me fix this one and re-check. Also the postponed Goiás-Corinthians 2022 (unplayed bras record + played brf record 14 days apart) — add the unplayed-merge rule to dedupe: within a pairing group (same season+competition), an unplayed record merges with the nearest played cluster.\n\nImplementation in _deduplicate: currently clusters by date chaining. Modify: after building clusters for a group, if there's an unplayed singleton cluster (or cluster where keeper has no goals) and other played clusters exist, merge the unplayed one into the NEAREST-date played cluster (prefer same source priority merge — the unplayed bras record merges into brf's played cluster? Keeper priority: bras(0) < brf(4) → keeper = bras record (unplayed, None goals) enriched with brf's goals/date? The merge fills keeper's None fields from other: goals filled from brf ✓, but date stays bras's original date (keeper date not None). Hmm — the played date should win. For the postponed case, the real played date is brf's. If keeper has date but the OTHER has goals... I should prefer the PLAYED record as keeper. Merge rule: keeper = played record with best source priority; if all unplayed → best priority. Let me implement: sort cluster candidates by (not played, SOURCE_PRIORITY) and pick keeper. Then fill fields. That handles it: brf played record wins over bras unplayed. But then stats (corners etc.) from brf ✓, round from bras ✓.\n\nWait, but there's a subtlety: keeper's date = brf's played date (2022-10-29) ✓ good.\n\nAlso for filling: if keeper is played but other has goals too and they disagree — keeper wins (priority) ✓ fine.\n\nLet me now fix the alias and the merge-keeper rule.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ab629f9001AzKd4bx65kXt3F","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05ab5db24001c4uCvk6BReXl36"}}
