eason == 2015 and m.source == \"br_football\" and (m.home, m.away) not in bras_pairs]\nfor m in extra:\n    print(m.date, m.home_display, m.home_goals, \"-\", m.away_goals, m.away_display)\n# and same pairing other dates in 2015\nfor m in extra:\n    same = [x for x in store.matches if x.competition == \"Brasileirão Série A\" and x.season == 2015 and {x.home, x.away} == {m.home, m.away}]\n    for s in same:\n        print(\"  same pairing:\", s.source, s.date, s.home_display, s.home_goals, \"-\", s.away_goals, s.away_display)\nEOF","time":{"start":1788228384319,"end":1788228384336}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now every Série A season has exactly 380 matches (2003-2005 have different formats: 552/552/462 ✓; 2023 has 377 as brf is incomplete; 2015 has 381 — one extra, the Jan/Feb 2016 brf record shifted to 2015).\n\nStandings validation against real history:\n- 2018: Palmeiras 80 ✓ (real: Palmeiras 80). Relegated: Sport, América-MG, Vitória, Paraná ✓ correct!\n- 2019: Flamengo 90 ✓. Relegated: Cruzeiro, CSA, Chapecoense, Avaí ✓ correct!\n- 2020: Flamengo 71 ✓ (real: Flamengo 71). Relegated: Vasco, Goiás, Coritiba, Botafogo ✓ correct! (earlier run showed Atlético-MG 74 champion — that was with the unmerged Vasco duplication bug; now fixed!)\n- 2021: Atlético-MG 84 ✓ (real: 84). Relegated: Grêmio, Bahia, Sport, Chapecoense ✓ correct!\n- 2022: Palmeiras 81 ✓ (real: 81). Relegated: Ceará, Goianiense, Avaí, Juventude ✓ correct!\n- 2023: Grêmio 68 — real 2023 champion was Palmeiras 82. brf 2023 data is incomplete/erroneous (377 matches; Palmeiras data shows 19W 10D 8L vs real 24W 11D 3L?). Hmm wait — if every team has ~38 games and scores are wrong for Palmeiras... Let me quickly check 2023: Palmeiras points? Real: 82. If our data says otherwise, the brf 2023 Serie A data itself is wrong (it's a CC0 crowd dataset). Let me verify one famous 2023 match to see if brf 2023 is garbage: e.g., 2023-04-29 round 1: Palmeiras 2-1 Cuiabá? Real round 1 2023: Palmeiras? Hmm I don't remember exactly. Let me look at Palmeiras 2023 matches in the data vs real record (24W 11D 3L, 82 pts, GF 68? GA 33). Our data: 19W 10D 8L 61GF 32GA in 37 games. That's clearly DIFFERENT from reality. So brf 2023 Série A is unreliable. Nothing I can do — the data is what it is. I'll note this in the README (2023 Série A from the BR-Football file appears partially inaccurate; 2012-2022 cross-validated).\n\nWait, actually let me double-check with the Copa do Brasil 2023: 'Sao Paulo 1-1 Flamengo 2023-09-24' — real 2023 CdB semifinal leg 1: São Paulo 1-0 Flamengo? Hmm. Not sure. The dataset is what it is.\n\n2015's 381: the single phantom from brf Jan/Feb 2016 record. Let me see what that record is — maybe I can see if it's a legit 2015 match misdated or junk. Actually, earlier I saw ('Serie A', '2016'): 1 match in Jan/Feb 2016. That match, relabeled to 2015 by my month≤2 rule, might duplicate a 2015 fixture at a different date (postponed match absorbed? it's PLAYED with goals). If it has a counterpart in the same pairing within 2015 → dedupe would merge if ≤4 days... it's +1 so it didn't merge. Let me look at it and decide: if it's junk, options: leave it (1 match — harmless, standings 2015 barely affected), or drop brf Jan/Feb Serie A matches with no authoritative counterpart. Hmm — dropping data is bad; leaving 1 phantom is fine. Actually wait — let me check whether it's really a duplicate of a 2015 fixture:","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ab7af96001BkrFz0JenjZAdT","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05ab74491001jM4ZVOPfkSvmGA"}}
