rie A' in brf. It involves teams not even in Série A 2015. It's junk relative to Série A but the pairing is unique so it adds +1 to \"Série A 2015\" standings (adds two phantom teams with 1 match).\n\nOptions: leave it (standings show 22 teams for 2015, bottom two being these phantom teams — actually that corrupts the \"relegated\" output for 2015!). Since relegated = bottom 4 of table, phantom teams with 1 point would occupy relegation spots. Let me check standings 2015 relegated: they'd be Brasilia FC + CA Taguatinga + 2 real ones ✗ WRONG.\n\nFix options:\na) For league standings (Série A/B/C), only include teams with a plausible number of matches (e.g., ≥ half the max matches of any team in that season table). A round-robin season: teams play 38 (or 46 in 2003-2004, 42 in 2005). Filter: matches >= 0.5 * max_matches. That's data-driven and robust. For 2015: max 38, threshold 19 → phantoms (1 match) excluded ✓. For 2023 (377 matches): max ~37-38 → teams with ≥19 ✓ fine. For Série B/C similar.\nb) Drop the record at load: brf 'Serie A' matches in Jan/Feb with no counterpart AND involving teams not otherwise in that season... too specific.\n\nOption (a) is clean and principled: standings filter to teams with ≥50% of the max matches played (round-robin regulars). Let me apply to standings() only (not best_records, which has min_matches param anyway).\n\nHmm — but wait: should I also handle \"relegated\" for 2003 (552 matches, 24 teams... relegated historically only 2 in 2003? Actually 2003 relegated 4? No — 2003: 2 relegated? The format: 2003-2005 had varying relegation (2003: 4 down? I recall 2003 relegated Fortaleza?...). The tool reports \"bottom 4\" labeled as relegation zone — for 2003-2005 that's approximate. Note in docstring. Fine for a demo tool.\n\nAlso check 2015 standings after the fix, plus 2023: with 377 matches, teams missing games — threshold 19 keeps all regular teams ✓.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: threshold 0.5*max — for Série A 2023, all 20 teams have ≥36 matches ✓. For 2015: 20 teams at 38, 2 phantoms at 1 → excluded ✓. \n\nImplement in standings(): compute records, then filter records where matches >= 0.5 * max_matches before sorting.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ab81275001PtKcAtLZO4hjvu","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05ab7b7b6001008WGhA9PhXTcc"}}
