b atletico lanus\", \"\"),\n+    \"club atletico colon\": (\"club atletico colon\", \"\"),\n+    \"club atletico tigre\": (\"club atletico tigre\", \"\"),\n+    \"club atletico talleres\": (\"club atletico talleres\", \"\"),\n+    \"club atletico huracan\": (\"club atletico huracan\", \"\"),\n+    \"club atletico banfield\": (\"club atletico banfield\", \"\"),\n+    \"club atletico aldosivi\": (\"club atletico aldosivi\", \"\"),\n }\n \n DEFAULT_UF: dict[str, str] = {\n     \"atletico\": \"PR\",\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/normalize.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -120,8 +120,16 @@\n     \"flamengo do piaui\": (\"flamengo\", \"PI\"),\n     \"guarani de juazeiro\": (\"guarani\", \"CE\"),\n     \"vitoria f c\": (\"vitoria\", \"ES\"),\n     \"vitoria es\": (\"vitoria\", \"ES\"),\n+    \"club america\": (\"club america\", \"\"),\n+    \"club atletico lanus\": (\"club atletico lanus\", \"\"),\n+    \"club atletico colon\": (\"club atletico colon\", \"\"),\n+    \"club atletico tigre\": (\"club atletico tigre\", \"\"),\n+    \"club atletico talleres\": (\"club atletico talleres\", \"\"),\n+    \"club atletico huracan\": (\"club atletico huracan\", \"\"),\n+    \"club atletico banfield\": (\"club atletico banfield\", \"\"),\n+    \"club atletico aldosivi\": (\"club atletico aldosivi\", \"\"),\n }\n \n DEFAULT_UF: dict[str, str] = {\n     \"atletico\": \"PR\",\n","additions":8,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"src/brasil_mcp/normalize.py","time":{"start":1788228487660,"end":1788228487662}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"2003: Cruzeiro 100 pts ✓ (real! Cruzeiro won 2003 with 100 pts). 2015: Corinthians 81 ✓ (real). Relagated 2015: Avaí, Vasco, Goiás, Joinville ✓ correct!\n\nDisplay names mostly good, but two issues:\n1. `america-mg` displays \"Club América\" — WRONG! That's the Mexican club! Why? Because `registry.observe(player.club)` in load_all observes FIFA clubs including \"Club América\" → parse 'club america' → filter 'club' → base 'america' → DEFAULT_UF 'america'→MG → 'america-mg'!! The Mexican Club América folded into america-mg! Then display picked unsuffixed 'Club América' (FIFA club count 30).\n\nFix: FIFA foreign clubs shouldn't use Brazilian DEFAULT_UF pins! The alias/DEFAULT approach is Brazil-centric. For FIFA club resolution I need country awareness: 'Club América' is Mexican. But the registry has no nationality info...\n\nBetter fix: don't observe FIFA foreign clubs into the same registry without distinction. The purpose of observing FIFA clubs: (1) resolve club filter queries, (2) link Brazilian squads to teams. The collision happens because bare base 'america' → pinned MG.\n\nTargeted fix: add alias 'club america' → its own canonical ('club america', None). Also 'america de cali' (Colombian) → parse: tokens [america, de, cali] → base 'america de cali' — own canonical ✓ no collision. 'Club América' → filter 'club' → 'america' → collision. Add aliases for the FIFA foreign clubs that collide with Brazilian bases:\n- 'club america' → ('club america', None)? Hmm wait — but also queries: user asking 'América' (Brazilian MG) works via DEFAULT. But FIFA club 'Club América' resolving to 'club america' separate canonical ✓ good.\n- 'athletic club' variants? 'Athletic Club MG' (brf, Brazilian!) — Athletic Club (São João del-Rey, MG) → base 'athletic' → filtered legal word 'athletic'?? LEGAL_WORDS includes 'athletic'! tokens [athletic, club, mg] → uf MG → [athletic, club] → filter → ['mg']?? wait uf extracted first: tokens [athletic, club] after MG removal → drop legal words → both 'athletic' and 'club' are legal words → kept=tokens (fallback keeps original when all filtered) → base 'athletic club' → 'athletic club-mg' ✓ OK distinct. And FIFA 'Athletic Club de Bilbao' → tokens [athletic, club, de, bilbao] → no uf → drop legal: 'athletic','club' filtered, 'de' kept (not in LEGAL_WORDS) → [de, bilbao] → base 'de bilbao' — ugly but harmless distinct canonical. Whatever, no collision.\n- 'vitoria guimaraes' → base 'vitoria guimaraes' distinct ✓. 'vitoria de setubal' → 'vitoria de setubal' ✓.\n- 'atletico nacional' → base 'atletico nacional' ✓ distinct from atletico-mg/pr/go.\n- 'atletico madrid' ✓ distinct. 'atletico bucaramanga' ✓. 'atletico tucuman' ✓. 'atletico huila' ✓.\n- 'santos laguna' ✓ distinct base.\n- 'america de cali' ✓ distinct.\n- So only 'Club América' collides → alias it.\n\nAlso should I worry about DEFAULT_UF resolving FOREIGN query names, e.g., user queries 'América' meaning Mexican? The store is Brazil-focused; DEFAULT→MG is the sensible interpretation for Brazilian soccer context. And 'Club América' exact alias handles the FIFA club.\n\n2. `bahia-ba` displays \"EC Bahia\" — prefer prettier 'Bahia'. The unsuffixed candidates: 'EC Bahia' (brf), 'Bahia' (brf? novo 'Bahia', lib 'Bahia'?). Display picked 'EC Bahia' — meaning 'Bahia' unsuffixed count < 'EC Bahia' count, or 'Bahia' is suffixed?? In novo, Bahia appears as 'Bahia' (no suffix) — novo 2003-2019 Bahia played ~7 seasons ≈ 260+ matches... but wait, novo∩bras dedupe keeps bras's display? No — display comes from registry._canonical_raws which counts ALL observations (pre-dedupe) ✓. brf 'EC Bahia' (2014-2023 Série A+B+C ≈ 400+?) vs novo 'Bahia' (2003, 2004, 2007, 2008, 2010, 2011, 2012?... ~350?) + lib 'Bahia' + brf 'Bahia'? If brf uses 'EC Bahia' consistently, it could outnumber. My sort: (-count, len) → 'EC Bahia' won on count. Hmm. To prefer cleaner names I could add a small beauty bias: penalize names containing legal-entity words in di