juventude-rs': MA share? Juventude-MA in brf Série C? share maybe 10-20% → 'EC Juventude'?? it showed 'EC Juventude' — again the legal-words display issue (brf 'EC Juventude' vs novo 'Juventude'). With the clean-name preference: 'Juventude' (novo, bare base ✓ clean) preferred over 'EC Juventude' (not clean) ✓.\n\nLet me implement the display preference with cleanliness first, then count:\n```python\ndef _is_clean_display(raw, base):  # base = canonical base (before -uf)\n    parsed_base, uf, country = parse_team_name(raw)\n    return parsed_base == base and uf is None and country is None\n```\nWait — for suffixed fallback displays (ambiguous bases) I also want clean-ish: 'América - MG' tidied → 'América-MG' ✓ already tidy. For 'america-mg' the fallback candidates: 'América-MG'(bras), 'America MG'(brf), 'América - MG'(cup) → tidy → count highest wins: brf 'America MG' (no accent, ~400) vs 'América-MG' — 'America MG' likely wins → display 'America MG'. Hmm, prefer accented when equally clean? Micro-aesthetics; skip — I'll normalize suffix form to hyphenated: replace r'\\s+-\\s+([A-Z]{2,3})$' → '-MG' AND r'\\s+([A-Z]{2})$' (space-suffixed like 'America MG') → '-MG'?? That changes 'Gremio RS' → 'Gremio-RS'. For display fallback: apply suffix tidying for both ' - XX' and ' XX' patterns. I'll do: match r'[-\\s]\\s*([A-Z]{2,3})$' → f'-\\1'.\n\nAlso 'flamengo-pi' minor club — display 'Flamengo-PI' ✓ fine.\n\nAnd 'atletico-mg' display 'Atlético-MG' ✓ nice (ambiguous base atletico → suffixed).\n\nLet me now implement:\n1. TEAM_ALIASES += 'club america': ('club america', '')... wait alias format is (base, uf) — uf empty string? canonical_id with uf None → 'club america' ✓. But my alias unpack `base, uf = TEAM_ALIASES[full_key]` then return base, uf, None — uf must be str|None. Use (\"club america\", \"\") → canonical_id('club america', '', None) → 'club america' ✓. Hmm canonical_id checks `if uf:` — empty string falsy ✓ → returns base ✓.\n\nActually wait — there's a subtlety: 'Club América' FIFA club observed → alias → canonical 'club america'. player_search(club='Club América') → resolve → 'club america' ✓. And query 'América' → 'america-mg' (Brazilian) — fine.\n\n2. Display preference rewrite in finalize().\n\nAlso fix 'nautico-pe' display showed 'Náutico' ✓ good already (unsuffixed 'Náutico' from novo exists, base unambiguous? nautico {PE, RR}: PE share high → unambiguous → 'Náutico' ✓).\n\n3. Threshold: keep 0.8 (defensible).\n\nAlso 'America RN' display for america-rn — ambiguous → suffixed fallback: raws 'America RN'(brf), 'América - RN'(cup), 'América-RN'(novo), 'América de Natal - RN'(cup) → tidy → 'America RN' or 'América-RN'... tidy handles ' - RN' and ' RN'?? ' RN' with single space — my regex r'[-\\s]\\s*([A-Z]{2,3})$' on 'America RN' → 'America-RN' ✓. On 'América-RN' already ✓. Count decides accent vs not — brf 'America RN' probably wins (no accent) → 'America-RN'. Fine.\n\nLet me implement these two fixes.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ab949e40019ij8uuny86dCdC","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05ab84542001zRsOsUyxhR5POY"}}
