me collides with a known European club? Over-engineering. Pragmatic: alias 'boavista' → ('boavista fc', '') meaning bare 'Boavista' (FIFA) is Portuguese; the Brazilian one becomes 'boavista sport-rj' via its full cup name. Then brazilian_clubs_with_squads drops it ✓ and players_at_club('Boavista') returns the Portuguese squad — defensible (FIFA data IS the Portuguese club). \n\n   Wait, but does the cup file contain other Boavista spellings? 'Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ' only (14 chars? it appeared 2x in sample). With paren stripped: 'boavista sport club - rj' → uf RJ → [boavista, sport, club] → alias? no → drop legal 'club' → [boavista, sport] → base 'boavista sport' → 'boavista sport-rj' ✓ self-consistent.\n\n2. 'Ceara' display lacks accent (should be 'Ceará'), 'Avai' → 'Avaí', 'Cuiaba' → 'Cuiabá'. Because clean-display candidates for ceara-ce: 'Ceara' (brf, most frequent) vs 'Ceará' (novo/cup). Count wins → unaccented brf form. Aesthetically suboptimal. Improvement: when multiple clean candidates exist, prefer the one with accents (i.e., more frequent accented form)? Tie-break by \"has non-ascii chars\" before count? Risky: could pick rare accented misspellings. Alternative: prefer the candidate that appears in the most distinct sources? Or prefer the most frequent among candidates that contain accents when the base's accented form is well-attested... Simple heuristic: among clean candidates, sort by (-count) but if the top candidate is pure-ASCII and another candidate within 50% of its count has accents, prefer the accented one. Implementation: pick top by count; then check accented alternatives with count >= 0.5 * top_count → prefer the most frequent accented one. 'Ceara' (brf ~300) vs 'Ceará' (novo+cup ~150?) → 150 >= 150 ✓ → 'Ceará'. 'Avai' (brf) vs 'Avaí' (bras 'Avai-SC' suffixed! cup 'Avaí - SC' suffixed; novo 'Avaí' clean!) → novo Avaí count ~2 seasons? Hmm ~70. brf 'Avai' Série A/B ~200+. 70 >= 100? No → 'Avai' stays unaccented ✗. Lower threshold to 0.3? 'America' vs 'América'... america-mg display is suffixed fallback anyway.\n\n   Honestly, this is cosmetic. A simpler robust approach: prefer the accented form when ANY accented clean candidate exists AND the base has a \"known accented\" canonical spelling... I could hard-code a small PREFERRED_DISPLAYS map for the major clubs: {'ceara-ce': 'Ceará', 'avai-sc': 'Avaí', 'cuiaba-mt': 'Cuiabá', 'goias-go': 'Goiás' (already ✓ via count), 'gremio-rs': 'Grêmio' ✓, ...}. That's clean and predictable: PREFERRED_DISPLAYS in normalize.py applied at the end of finalize(). For: ceara-ce → 'Ceará', avai-sc → 'Avaí', cuiaba-mt → 'Cuiabá', vitoria-ba → 'Vitória', america-mg → 'América-MG', america-rn → 'América-RN', atletico-mg → 'Atlético-MG', atletico-pr → 'Athletico-PR' (the modern name — already shows Athletico-PR ✓), botafogo-rj → 'Botafogo' hmm — leave suffixed (it's genuinely ambiguous with PB)... spec examples show 'Botafogo' plain; but ambiguity — keep 'Botafogo-RJ'. 'parana-pr' → 'Paraná'. 'flamengo-pi' leave. 'juventude-rs' → 'Juventude' ✓ already. 'coritiba-pr' → 'Coritiba' ✓. 'nautico-pe' ✓ 'Náutico'. 'santa cruz-pe' → 'Santa Cruz'. 'ceara'... ok.\n\nLet me add PREFERRED_DISPLAYS for these specific cases.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05aba9ecd001UR8zWPOiDdwkxq","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05aba1393001tijAGpBUeuO7QQ"}}
