ches\", {\"team\": \"Flamengo\", \"opponent\": \"Fluminense\", \"limit\": 3})\n                for item in result.content:\n                    print(\"\\n--- search_matches result:\")\n                    print(item.text[:800] if hasattr(item, 'text') else item)\n                result2 = await session.call_tool(\"standings\", {\"season\": 2019})\n                print(\"\\n--- standings result:\")\n                print(result2.content[0].text[:400] if hasattr(result2.content[0], 'text') else result2.content[0])\n                tg.cancel_scope.cancel()\n\nanyio.run(run)\nEOF","time":{"start":1788228811682,"end":1788228811739}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Everything is working beautifully:\n- 2019 standings exactly match the spec's example format AND real history (Flamengo 90, Santos 74, Palmeiras 74 ✓)\n- Derbies, players, squads all work\n- H2H works\n\nInteresting: the FIFA Grêmio squad has fictional-ish names (Ronaldo Cabrais, Josué Chiamulera) — that's the FIFA dataset's generic players for unlicensed clubs. Fine, data is data.\n\nNote: \"Matches for Palmeiras Série A 2023 season:\" — filter description missing \"in\": \"for Palmeiras Série A 2023 season\" is a bit clunky but OK.\n\nNow let me test the MCP server itself with the in-memory client, then write the test suite. First quick server test.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05abe337e001k1gx0vhLu3IpRO","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05abe0284001g97mEroe28kc2z"}}
