Corinthians home 2022\nstats = store.team_stats(\"Corinthians\", season=2022)\nprint(\"Corinthians 2022 home:\", stats[\"home\"])\nprint(\"Corinthians 2022 overall:\", {k: stats['overall'][k] for k in ('matches','wins','draws','losses','goals_for','goals_against')})\n\n# Copa do Brasil 2012 final\nmatches, total = store.find_matches(competition=\"Copa do Brasil\", season=2012, stage=\"final\", limit=None)\nprint(\"\\nCopa 2012 finals:\", [(m.date, m.home_display, m.home_goals, m.away_goals, m.away_display, m.round) for m in matches])\n\n# Libertadores 2019 final\nmatches, total = store.find_matches(competition=\"Libertadores\", season=2019, stage=\"final\", limit=None)\nprint(\"Lib 2019 finals:\", [(m.date, m.home_display, m.home_goals, m.away_goals, m.away_display) for m in matches])\n\n# biggest wins overall\nwins = store.biggest_wins(limit=5)\nprint(\"\\nBiggest wins:\")\nfor m in wins: print(\"  \", m.date, m.home_display, m.home_goals, \"-\", m.away_goals, m.away_display, \"|\", m.competition)\n\n# goals analysis Serie A\nga = store.goals_analysis(competition=\"Série A\")\nprint(\"\\nSérie A goals:\", ga)\n\n# best away records all-time\nba = store.best_records(venue=\"away\", min_matches=100, limit=5)\nprint(\"\\nBest away records:\", [(r['team'], r['ppg']) for r in ba])\n\n# Fla-Flu totals\nh = store.head_to_head(\"Flamengo\", \"Fluminense\")\nprint(\"\\nFla-Flu:\", h[\"team_a\"][\"wins\"], h[\"team_b\"][\"wins\"], h[\"team_a\"][\"draws\"], \"matches:\", h[\"team_a\"][\"matches\"])\n\n# Brazilians count\nplayers, total = store.player_search(nationality=\"Brazil\", limit=1)\nprint(\"Brazilians in FIFA data:\", total)\n\n# Alisson\np, t = store.player_search(name=\"Alisson\", limit=5)\nprint(\"Alisson:\", [(x.name, x.club, x.overall, x.position) for x in p])\n\n# Gabriel Barbosa (not in data)\np, t = store.player_search(name=\"Gabriel Barbosa\", limit=5)\nprint(\"Gabriel Barbosa:\", t)\n\n# last Flamengo vs Corinthians match\nmatches, total = store.find_matches(team=\"Flamengo\", opponent=\"Corinthians\", limit=1)\nprint(\"\\nLast Fla x Corinthians:\", matches[0].label() if matches else None)\n\n# 2023 derbies count\nd = store.derbies(season=2023)\nprint(\"2023 derbies:\", {k: len(v) for k, v in d.items()})\nEOF","time":{"start":1788228851260,"end":1788228851276}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The MCP server works end-to-end: 14 tools listed, tools callable, results serialized as JSON with summaries. \n\nNow I'll write the test suite — BDD-style per the spec's testing approach. Structure:\n\n```\ntests/\n  conftest.py            — session-scoped store fixture, client session helper\n  test_dates.py          — date parsing unit tests\n  test_normalize.py      — team name canonicalization unit tests\n  test_loaders.py        — all 6 files load with expected counts\n  test_bdd_match_queries.py      — Gherkin scenarios (Feature header comments)\n  test_bdd_team_queries.py\n  test_bdd_player_queries.py\n  test_bdd_competition_queries.py\n  test_bdd_statistics.py\n  test_bdd_sample_questions.py   — 20+ natural-language question matrix\n  test_server.py          — MCP integration via in-memory client\n```\n\nThe BDD style: use Gherkin-style docstrings/comments with Given/When/Then structure. I'll write tests in clear GWT form — each scenario as a test function with GIVEN/WHEN/THEN comments and asserts. This matches the spec's \"Use BDD test scenarios\" requirement.\n\nconftest.py:\n```python\nimport pytest\nfrom brasil_mcp.store import SoccerStore, default_data_dir\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef store():\n    return SoccerStore(default_data_dir())\n```\n\nFor the server test, an async fixture with anyio/pytest — anyio pytest plugin is bundled with anyio (anyio.pytest_plugin). `@pytest.mark.anyio` needs the anyio_backend fixture. Simpler: run the async client test with anyio.run inside a sync test.\n\nFacts to assert (from data, verified):\n- Loader counts: bras 4180, cup 1337, lib 1255, brf 10296, novo 6886, fifa 18207.\n- Dates: parse_date('2023-09-24'), '29/03/2003' → date(2003,3,29), '2012-05-19 18:30:00' → date(2012,5,19), 'NA' → None.\n- Normalize: 'Palmeiras-SP' == 'Palmeiras' == 'PALMEIRAS' == 'palmeiras sp'; 'Athletico-PR' == 'Atlético - PR' == 'Atlético Paranaense'; 'Santos' != 'Santos-AP' != 'Santos Laguna'; 'Sport Club Corinthians Paulista' → corinthians-sp; 'Vasco da Gama-RJ' == 'Vasco'; 'Clube de Regatas do Flamengo' == Flamengo.\n- Matches: Flamengo vs Fluminense ≥ 40 matches; each has date/competition/scores; sorted newest first; 2019 season filter → 2 matches (brs) + maybe more from dedupe... let me be careful — assert ≥1 and competition labels.\n- Copa do Brasil finals: stage='final' → matches from max round per season; 2012 final: Palmeiras? The 2012 CdB final was Palmeiras vs Coritiba (Palmeiras won). Test: search cup finals 2012 → 2 matches Palmeiras vs Coritiba. Let me verify from data before writing.\n- Libertadores finals: stage='final' → 2019 final: Flamengo 2-1 River Plate (single match). Verify.\n- team_stats: Palmeiras 2023 → 37 matches (19W 10D 8L, 61:32). Corinthians home 2022: compute. Let me verify numbers from the built store before writing assertions.\n- standings: 2019 → Flamengo 90 pts champion, relegated 4 = Cruzeiro/CSA/Chapecoense/Avaí; table length 20; internal consistency: sum of wins*3+draws == points; everyone 38 matches.\n- 2020 champion Flamengo 71.\n- players: 'Neymar Jr' overall 92; nationality Brazil → 827 players... wait earlier count said 827. Verify with search: total for nationality=Brazil without limit... 827? The earlier count was Counter of Nationality == 'Brazil' → 827 ✓. Club 'Santos' → 20 players; club 'Santos Laguna' → 26 (players at the Mexican club); 'Santos' club search must NOT include Laguna players. position forward group; name search 'Alisson' → goalkeeper at Liverpool 85.\n- team_players('Flamengo') → empty + helpful note; team_players('Santos') → 20.\n- biggest wins: top margins; spec example mentions \"Santos 8-0 Bolivar (Libertadores)\" hmm — actually check the top win in data. \n- goals_analysis Série A: avg ~2.4; home win rate > away win rate.\n- best_records away: Palmeiras/Flamengo ranks; internal: ppg descending.\n- derbies 2023: Fla-Flu ≥ 2 matches.\n- compare_teams: Palmeiras vs Santos summary contains both records and H2H.\n- find_team('sport club corinthians paulista') → Corinthians with matches > 0.\n- Sample questions matrix (20+): table-driven pytest.mark.parametrize with (question, tool, kwargs, checker).\n\nMCP server test: list_tools ≥ 14; call search_matches + standings + search_players; verify summary strings.\n\nPerformance tests (spec: simple lookups < 2s, aggregates < 5s): time a few calls after warm load — but the store load itself takes 1.6s; queries themselves are fast (in-memory). I'll assert query execution times on the warm store (excluding load).\n\nLet me first collect the remaining ground-truth facts to assert (Corinthians home 2022, Copa 2012 final, Libertadores 2019 final, biggest wins top, Flamengo 2023 matches count, goal analysis numbers, best away record).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05abecf27001tNwEqYQ23y8Vqc","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05abe3d3b001kviUBOuaWLBGex"}}
