{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788228877465,"sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_76888e019f31477b888d3745","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Shared fixtures for the BDD test suite.\n\nThe store is session-scoped: loading the six CSVs takes ~1.5s, so all\nscenarios share one SoccerStore instance.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom brasil_mcp import queries\nfrom brasil_mcp.store import SoccerStore, default_data_dir\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef store() -> SoccerStore:\n    return SoccerStore(default_data_dir())\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef loaded_store(store) -> SoccerStore:\n    \"\"\"Alias used by Gherkin 'Given the match data is loaded' steps.\"\"\"\n    return store\n\n\nTOOL_ROUTER = {\n    \"find_team\": queries.find_team,\n    \"search_matches\": queries.search_matches,\n    \"head_to_head\": queries.head_to_head,\n    \"team_stats\": queries.team_stats,\n    \"team_season_history\": queries.team_season_history,\n    \"standings\": queries.standings,\n    \"search_players\": queries.search_players,\n    \"team_players\": queries.team_players,\n    \"competition_info\": queries.competition_info,\n    \"derbies\": queries.derbies,\n    \"biggest_wins\": queries.biggest_wins,\n    \"goals_analysis\": queries.goals_analysis,\n    \"best_records\": queries.best_records,\n    \"compare_teams\": queries.compare_teams,\n}\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef ask():\n    \"\"\"Dispatch a natural-language-backed tool call by tool name.\"\"\"\n\n    def _ask(tool: str, **kwargs) -> dict:\n        return TOOL_ROUTER[tool](**kwargs)\n\n    return _ask\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/tests/conftest.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/tests/conftest.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"tests/conftest.py","time":{"start":1788228877456,"end":1788228877461}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait — Corinthians 2022: 58 matches?! 38 league + Copa do Brasil + Libertadores = Corinthians played 2022: Série A 38 + CdB ~6 + Libertadores ~10 + Sudamericana? That's plausible (58 total across competitions). But home = 29 matches in 2022? Série A home 19 + CdB home 3 + Lib home 5 = 27... 29 fine (all competitions). The spec example asks \"Corinthians home record in 2022\" — our answer covers all competitions; a competition param can narrow it. OK.\n\nAlso Corinthians home 2022 shows \"matches: 29\" — hmm, but the \"home\" record counts only home matches ✓.\n\nCopa 2012 final: Palmeiras 2-0 Coritiba & Coritiba 1-1 Palmeiras ✓ (real history: Palmeiras won 2012 CdB ✓). Round '6'?? The max round for 2012 is 6 — wait, but round 8 existed for other seasons. 2012 had 6 rounds? Hmm — earlier round counter: round 8 x14. 2012 final = round 6?? Hmm, wait — actually looking at output: round '6' for the 2012 final legs. But hold on, that contradicts \"round 8 = final\". Let me recheck: _cup_final_rounds[2012] = max round in 2012 = 6? The 2012 cup had rounds 1-6? Hmm — actually 2012 Copa do Brasil: 6 rounds? But then what's round 7/8 in other seasons? Different seasons have different round counts (7 or 8). max round per season = final round ✓ works per season. But wait — 2012 final legs are round 6, but 2012 also has rounds 1-5 ✓ consistent.\n\nHmm wait, actually there's an issue: round 6 in 2012 = final. But in seasons with 8 rounds, round 6 = quarterfinals? Let me sanity check 2013: max round? Whatever — per-season max = final ✓ data-driven, correct.\n\nBUT: is 2012 final really round 6? Real 2012 CdB final was Palmeiras vs Coritiba ✓ July 2012 ✓. The dates shown (July 5 leg1 Palmeiras home, July 11 leg2 Coritiba home) ✓ correct!\n\nLibertadores 2019 final: Flamengo 2-1 River Plate, single match Nov 23 2019 ✓ correct!\n\nBiggest wins: São Paulo 9-1 4 de Julho (CdB 2021?) — actually that's plausible (CdB first round mismatches).\n\nEverything checks out. Now — one more check on `team_stats` for Corinthians 2022 with 58 matches: the \"home\" record 29 includes cup/lib. Spec example: \"Corinthians home record (2022 Brasileirão): Matches: 19\" — so tests should use competition filter for league-only. team_stats(\"Corinthians\", season=2022, competition=\"Série A\")[\"home\"] → 19 matches. Let me confirm quickly in the test.\n\nAlso best away: Palmeiras 1.33 ppg — the spec asks \"Which team has the best away record?\" ✓.\n\nNow write the tests. Plan (BDD GWT style with Gherkin feature docstrings):\n\nconftest.py — session store fixture + `ask` helper that calls query functions via a dispatch dict (shared with sample questions test).\n\nLet me write all test files now. Also add performance smoke assertions (simple <2s, aggregate <5s per spec).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05abf3c8a001ndBIoFzMrXD1bX","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05abed7ac0014A02Gr6WZ2p59p"}}
