===================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/queries.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-ce22193d1e90/src/brasil_mcp/queries.py\n@@ -86,8 +86,9 @@\n     \"aliases\": store.registry.aliases_of(cid)[:10],\n     \"total_matches\": total,\n     \"seasons\": seasons,\n     \"competitions\": competitions,\n+    \"titles\": trophies,\n     \"squad_size\": len(squad),\n }\n \n \n","additions":1,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"src/brasil_mcp/queries.py","time":{"start":1788228995797,"end":1788228995799}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait — `test_find_team_reports_championships` asserts `result.get(\"titles\", [])` but my find_team function returns trophies only in the summary lines, not as a \"titles\" key. Let me check queries.find_team: it builds `trophies` list and adds to lines but doesn't include in the returned dict. I should add \"titles\": trophies to the return. Also iterating ALL seasons for standings to find championships is expensive: Flamengo has seasons 2003-2023 → ~20 standings computations, each scanning matches... standings() calls find_matches(competition, season) which iterates all 18k matches per season → 20 × 18k = 360k iterations, fine (<1s). But it's called for every find_team — acceptable.\n\nHmm wait, actually there's a bug risk: find_team computes trophies by comparing table[\"champion\"][\"team\"] == display name. Champion team display must equal store.team_display(cid). In standings, the champion's display comes from match.home_display/away_display of that season — which should be the same display. But careful: team_display(cid) uses the global display; match.home_display is registry.display at load time — same function ✓.\n\nAlso titles list: for Flamengo — 2009? Flamengo won 2009! novo data covers 2009 ✓ → trophies should include 2009 and 2019, and 2020. Real: Flamengo champions 2009, 2019, 2020. Our data: 2009 standings from novo — Flamengo won 2009 with 67 pts... let me verify in the test run. The test asserts \"2019 Brasileirão Série A\" in titles ✓ should pass regardless.\n\nLet me add \"titles\" to find_team return. Also fix test file name conventions. Let me also double check `test_most_goals_in_serie_a_2023` — asserting top is one of several plausible teams (data-dependent). Fine.\n\nNow update queries.find_team to include titles.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ac10aca001D8EP379Qj1DerB","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05ac0d2f2001nZRuhOqq44Kd29"}}
