2-2022 includes 2013 → fails. Ha! My test is historically wrong. Palmeiras: relegated 2012, Série B 2013. Use another team with continuous presence... Flamengo? Never relegated (well, 2005 paper relegation aside — in 2012-2022 Flamengo always Série A). But wait the earlier failure output showed `test_every_season_has_matches` failed — yes, Palmeiras 2013 = 0 or the Série B matches don't count.\n\nAlso `test_season_coverage`: rows[SERIE_A]['seasons'] == '2003-2023' — with the 2023 season present (377 matches) — Série A seasons 2003-2023 ✓... but failure says otherwise. Maybe the junk 2015 phantom: 'Brasilia FC x CA Taguatinga' 2016-01-30 relabeled season 2015 ✓ still 2015... seasons range still 2003-2023. Hmm, why did it fail? Let me look at each failure. Also `test_2021_copa_do_brasil_final_round` — pairings: I asserted Grêmio-Palmeiras for 2021 finals. But the 2021 CdB final was actually... 2021 Copa do Brasil final: Atlético-MG vs Athletico-PR! (Nov 2021, Atlético won). The Grêmio-Palmeiras final was the 2020 final (played Mar 2021)! The CUP FILE labels it season 2020. So for season=2021, the final should be Atlético-MG x Athletico-PR. My test was wrong.\n\nAnd `test_brazilian_clubs_with_squads`: 'Boavista' in names — wait, the helpful-note failure message listed \"Boavista, América...\" — that's from `brazilian_clubs_with_squads()` which should EXCLUDE boavista-rj now... unless the canonical changed! With alias 'boavista sport' → ('boavista','RJ') and bare 'boavista' → base_ufs boavista {RJ} → boavista-rj. FIFA club 'Boavista' excluded by FOREIGN_FIFA_CLUBS ✓. But brf has bare 'Boavista' (3 matches, Brazilian Serie C/D club) — that's a DIFFERENT Boavista? 'Boavista SC Saquarema' aliased → boavista-rj; bare 'Boavista' in brf → boavista-rj (Brazilian) → then boavista-rj HAS matches ✓ still in list. Damn — the brf bare 'Boavista' is probably the SAQUAREMA club (Brazilian), so boavista-rj is legitimately a Brazilian club with matches, but its \"squad\" came from FIFA