{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788230097224,"sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_f6cb3096eccc467eb4b0f918","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"source venv/bin/activate && ruff check src/ tests/ --select E,F,W,I --line-length 110 && python -m pytest tests/ -q 2>&1 | tail -2","timeout":300000},"output":"All checks passed!\n........................................................................ [ 83%]\n............................                                             [100%]\n","metadata":{"output":"All checks passed!\n........................................................................ [ 83%]\n............................                                             [100%]\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"source venv/bin/activate && ruff check src/ tests/ --select E,F,W,I --line-length 110 && python -m pytest tests/ -q 2>&1 | tail -2","time":{"start":1788230097221,"end":1788230097223}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait — one subtle issue with the simplified `_team`: after `registry.observe(raw)` for an unknown name, `registry.resolve(raw)` still returns None if the base is unknown (base not in _base_ufs → wait, observe ADDS it to _base_ufs!). observe() → base in _base_ufs now → resolve → `_resolve_uf` → None (no distinct) → `if base in self._base_ufs: return base` → returns base ✓. So the second resolve works for any non-empty base. The final fallback only triggers for empty bases. Also display: registry.display(cid) for a fresh cid → _displays not rebuilt after observe (finalize not called) → falls back to `cid.replace('-',' ').title()` — acceptable for standalone loader use; in load_all flow finalize() runs first.\n\nHmm wait, actually there's one more edge: resolve() returning None happens when parse gives empty base — then parse_team_name again → empty → cid = \"\" → display(\"\") → \"\". Empty team name shouldn't occur in data (all names non-empty). Fine.\n\nNow re-run tests to make sure nothing broke, then finish with the final complete verification.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ad184d10013INUs2kUF3WTML","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","messageID":"msg_05ad14d98001KeOzkdepzT3O6u"}}
