{"type":"text","timestamp":1788230189668,"sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","part":{"id":"prt_05ad324f70014I7v4fgAVO58hy","messageID":"msg_05ad310be0011zzUCqpakP6yFn","sessionID":"ses_fa566b1a7ffetmaN0ZgRQlI0ol","type":"text","text":"Implementation complete. Summary of what was built:\n\n**MCP server** (`src/brasil_mcp/`, installable via `pip install -e .`):\n- **14 MCP tools** covering all 5 required capability categories: match/team/player/competition queries plus statistical analysis (standings, head-to-head, derbies, biggest wins, goals analysis, best records, team comparison)\n- **Data pipeline**: all 6 CSVs load in ~1.5s into a unified in-memory store with team indexes; every tool returns a spec-formatted `summary` string plus structured JSON\n\n**Key data-engineering challenges solved**:\n- **Team-name canonicalization**: folds `Palmeiras-SP` / `Palmeiras` / `Sport Club Corinthians Paulista` / FIFA full names onto one canonical id, while keeping true distinct clubs apart (`Santos` ≠ `Santos-AP` ≠ `Santos Laguna`)\n- **Cross-file dedup**: the 2012-2019 Série A exists in 3 files with conflicting dates — merged via pairing keys + 4-day proximity windows, yielding exactly 380 matches per season\n- **COVID season boundaries**: brf's calendar-year labels corrected (the 2020 final played in March 2021 → season 2020), so computed champions match real history (Cruzeiro 2003 w/ 100 pts, Flamengo 2019 w/ 90 pts & 2020, Atlético-MG 2021, Palmeiras 2022, correct relegation zones)\n\n**Verification**: 172 BDD-style tests pass (~21s, ~85% coverage) — including Gherkin scenarios from the spec, 28 sample questions answered end-to-end, MCP protocol integration over in-memory transport, real stdio JSON-RPC smoke test, CLI tests for all subcommands, and the spec's performance assertions (<2s lookups, <5s aggregates). Lint clean.\n\nRun it with `python -m brasil_mcp.server` (MCP stdio), `brasil-soccer-mcp`, or query directly via `brasil-soccer standings --season 2019`.","time":{"start":1788230182135,"end":1788230189665}}}
